300785cf34'}, {'abstract': 'Sam Ezersky wishes us all a happy April Fools’ Day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/31/crosswords/daily-puzzle-2021-04-01.html', 'snippet': 'Sam Ezersky wishes us all a happy April Fools’ Day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THURSDAY PUZZLE — It doesn’t happen every year, but once in a while the puzzle editors like to throw solvers a curveball on April 1. The most notable one — at least while I’ve been here — was in 2016, when Peter Gordon made a puzzle containing the message, “DUE TO BUDGET CUTS, THE NEW YORK TIMES CROSSWORD PUZZLE WILL END TOMORROW.” I thought that this was a hilarious April Fools’ joke that no one would possibly take seriously, so the Wordplay column for that day played along.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/05/crosswords/05wordplay-ticket/05wordplay-ticket-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/05/crosswords/05wordplay-ticket/05wordplay-ticket-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/05/crosswords/05wordplay-ticket/05wordplay-ticket-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/05/crosswords/05wordplay-ticket/05wordplay-ticket-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/05/crosswords/05wordplay-ticket/05wordplay-ticket-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/05/crosswords/05wordplay-ticket/05wordplay-ticket-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/05/crosswords/05wordplay-ticket/05wordplay-ticket-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Quite a Job, You Have to Admit', 'kicker': 'wordplay, the crossword column', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-01T02:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00af6e8b-e878-5a30-8979-1fb78b91db8d', 'word_count': 1347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00af6e8b-e878-5a30-8979-1fb78b91db8d'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections that appeared in print on Thursday, April 1, 2021.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/31/corrections/corrections-april-1-2021.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections that appeared in print on Thursday, April 1, 2021.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An article on Monday about the revival of hunting and trapping certain predators in Montana misstated how Gov. Greg Gianforte of Montana characterized his trapping experience. He said he had been trapping since he was a “tot,” not that he had been trapping wolves since that time. Because of editing errors, the article also described incorrectly the state and one of its senators. Montana is the third least dense state in the country, not the third least populous; and Steve Daines is the state’s junior senator, not its senior senator.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: April 1, 2021', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-04-01T02:19:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8aacdd4-7930-561e-a705-b50bcc285add', 'word_count': 349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8aacdd4-7930-561e-a705-b50bcc285add'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Thursday, April 1, 2021.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/31/todayspaper/quotation-of-the-day-euphoria-and-sorrow-as-nursing-homes-reopen-a-year-later.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Thursday, April 1, 2021.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I thought I would be so happy. And I just feel such grief because of the year of time I have lost and I will never get back.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: Euphoria and Sorrow as Nursing Homes Reopen a Year Later', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-04-01T02:21:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c4e43ec-4475-530f-8967-411a658a24a0', 'word_count': 61, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c4e43ec-4475-530f-8967-411a658a24a0'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. LaHood did not disclose the check on two government ethics forms, federal prosecutors said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/31/us/ray-lahood-billionaire-check.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. LaHood did not disclose 