isted of a long series of quiet mornings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/01/books/review/firekeepers-daughter-angeline-boulley.html', 'snippet': '“Firekeeper’s Daughter” is a runaway success, but the years leading to its publication consisted of a long series of quiet mornings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EARLY BIRD Wunderkind novelists are fun to hoot and holler about, but late bloomers deserve a solemn moment of silence. Let’s offer one up for Angeline Boulley, a 55-year-old mother of three, who toiled over "Firekeeper’s Daughter” for 10 years — during her son’s hockey practices and in work meetings; through seasons of celebration (including her kids’ high school and college graduations); and periods of tumult (a move from Sault Ste. Marie, Mich., to Washington, D.C., a divorce).', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/11/books/review/11InsidetheList-web/11InsidetheList-print-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/11/books/review/11InsidetheList-web/11InsidetheList-print-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 736}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/11/books/review/11InsidetheList-web/11InsidetheList-print-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 836, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/11/books/review/11InsidetheList-web/11InsidetheList-print-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1671, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/11/books/review/11InsidetheList-we