}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26290645-de4e-5430-a65d-4a56d899d4a9', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26290645-de4e-5430-a65d-4a56d899d4a9'}, {'abstract': 'Without a public eye, who are we?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/02/opinion/transgender-nonbinary-pandemic-transition-.html', 'snippet': 'Without a public eye, who are we?', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the world went into lockdown five months after I started taking testosterone, I thought it would be easier not to see people for a while. Maybe they wouldn’t hear my voice go scratchy or see up close the hormonal acne splattered across my face. Alone in my apartment, I imagined that all my difficulties in being seen and recognized as transgender-nonbinary would evaporate. No one would gender me except myself; my pronouns would be right there in the text box on my Zoom screen.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/04/opinion/sunday/02marzano_2/02marzano_2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 912, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/04/opinion/sunday/02marzano_2/02marzano_2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 912}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/04/opinion/sunday/02marzano_2/02marzano_2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 674, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/04/opinion/sunday/02marzano_2/02marzano_2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1348, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/04/opinion/sunday/0