nk': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f97aab10-97a6-54ca-9383-431f799b4e95', 'word_count': 1140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f97aab10-97a6-54ca-9383-431f799b4e95'}, {'abstract': 'The coronavirus and Brazil’s far-right president, Jair Bolsonaro, are jeopardizing the survival of Indigenous peoples and the future of the next human generation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/02/opinion/international-world/juma-people-brazil-amazon.html', 'snippet': 'The coronavirus and Brazil’s far-right president, Jair Bolsonaro, are jeopardizing the survival of Indigenous peoples and the future of the next human generation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Feb. 17, Aruká Juma, the last surviving man of the Juma people in the Brazilian Amazon, died of Covid-19 in a hospital in Pôrto Velho, the capital of Rondônia State, in northern Brazil. Mr. Juma, who was born in the 1930s in a jungle village on the Açuã River roughly 450 miles from the Amazonas State capital, Manaus, represented his community and their world. He was like the giant trees of the Amazon, and he fell.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/opinion/31Brum/31Brum-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 344, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/31/opinion/31Brum/31Brum-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 344}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/opinion/31Brum/31Brum-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 587, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/opinion/31Brum/31Brum-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1173, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/opinion/31Brum/31Brum-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/31/opinion/31Brum/31Brum-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/31/opinion/31Brum/31Brum-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Death of the Last Juma Elder in the Amazon', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Covid-19 Killed the Last Juma Elder in the Amazon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Juma, Aruka (d 2021)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMAZON JUNGLE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indigenous People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolsonaro, Jair (1955- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-02T19:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Opinion | The World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eliane Brum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eliane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e141290-a71d-51ba-8bb3-ce6748535387', 'word_count': 1349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e141290-a71d-51ba-8bb3-ce6748535387'}, {'abstract': 'Both children and parents do better when they have access to nutrition, health care and economic opportunity. Why not provide them all in one place?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/02/opinion/coronavirus-school-children-parents.html', 'snippet': 'Both children and parents do better when they have access to nutrition, health care and economic opportunity. Why not provide them all in one place?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In March of last year, the week before the pandemic shuttered schools in Washington, D.C., Annie Macheel’s Advanced Adult English as a Second Language class at Briya Public Charter School in Fort Totten was making plans. At one table, four women — two native Spanish-speakers, one Amharic speaker, and one Vietnamese speaker — haltingly practiced scheduling play dates for their children in English. Outside, in the hall, a group of pre-kindergartners — some of whom had mothers at that table — cheerfully burbled past the door, “caminando, caminando, volando, volando” (walking, walking, flying, flying).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/05/opinion/05fixes-williams-sub/02fixes-williams-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 780, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/05/opinion/05fixes-williams-sub/02fixes-williams-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 780}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/05/opinion/05fixes-williams-sub/02fixes-williams-sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 788, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/05/opinion/05fixes-williams-sub/02fixes-williams-sub-superJumbo