: 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-02T22:14:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Giovanni Russonello and Patricia Mazzei', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Giovanni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Russonello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mazzei', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/797f0624-89cd-55e9-940f-bbfbe3729ae0', 'word_count': 919, 'uri': 'nyt://article/797f0624-89cd-55e9-940f-bbfbe3729ae0'}, {'abstract': 'Brioni’s Norbert Stumpfl has approached his family’s home with characteristic patience and attention to detail.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/02/t-magazine/brioni-rome-minimalism-design.html', 'snippet': 'Brioni’s Norbert Stumpfl has approached his family’s home with characteristic patience and attention to detail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One understandable reaction to spending more time at home is to stockpile objects meant to provide comfort. Probably even dedicated minimalists have pondered, as of late, what another throw or accent pillow might do for their space and mental state. But, while he is certainly not averse to an elegant sort of ease, Norbert Stumpfl, the executive design director of the Italian men’s wear label Brioni, has always put a great deal of time and care into his aesthetic choices, with results that are so precise as to feel inevitable. This is apparent from his clothing collections, consisting of expertly tailored, handmade suits and separates in luxurious wools and silks — and from the three-story, 3,200-square-foot townhouse in central Rome where the Austria-born designer, 44, lives with his wife, Daphne Karras, a ceramist, and their two daughters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/12/27/t-magazine/27tmag-stumpfl-slide-6VN4/27tmag-stumpfl-slide-6VN4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/12/27/t-magazine/27tmag-stumpfl-slide-6VN4/27tmag-stumpfl-slide-6VN4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/12/27/t-magazine/27tmag-stumpfl-slide-6VN4/27tmag-stumpfl-slide-6VN4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/12/27/t-magazine/27tmag-stumpfl-slide-6VN4/27tmag-stumpfl-slide-6VN4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/12/27/t-magazine/27tmag-stumpfl-slide-6VN4/27tmag-stumpfl-slide-6VN4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/12/27/t-magazine/27tmag-stumpfl-slide-6VN4/27tmag-stumpfl-slide-6VN4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/12/27/t-magazine/27tmag-stumpfl-slide-6VN4/27tmag-stumpfl-slide-6VN4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150,