l', 'snippet': 'In “The Hard Crowd,” Kushner writes about two of her pet subjects — motorcycles and cars — as well as art, literature, politics and her formative years in San Francisco.', 'lead_paragraph': '“America was a V-8 country, gas-driven and water-cooled,” Harry Crews wrote in “Car,” his 1972 novel. In her first book of essays, “The Hard Crowd,” the novelist Rachel Kushner reminds us that she writes as well as any writer alive about the pleasure of a good motor doing what it was designed to do.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/06/books/review/05BOOKKUSHNER1/05BOOKKUSHNER1-articleLarge.png', 'height': 841, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/06/books/review/05BOOKKUSHNER1/05BOOKKUSHNER1-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 841}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/06/books/review/05BOOKKUSHNER1/05BOOKKUSHNER1-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 731, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/06/books/review/05BOOKKUSHNER1/05BOOKKUSHNER1-superJumbo.png', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1461, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/06/books/review/05BOOKKUSHNER1/05BOOKKUSHNER1-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/06/books/review/05BOOKKUSHNER1/05BOOKKUSHNER1-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':