ary to department policy and training.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/05/multimedia/05chauvin-trial-blog-arradondo/merlin_183891729_17e8f1ce-af5e-462b-bc4a-08d4ebc7bb22-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/05/multimedia/05chauvin-trial-blog-arradondo/merlin_183891729_17e8f1ce-af5e-462b-bc4a-08d4ebc7bb22-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/05/multimedia/05chauvin-trial-blog-arradondo/merlin_183891729_17e8f1ce-af5e-462b-bc4a-08d4ebc7bb22-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/05/multimedia/05chauvin-trial-blog-arradondo/merlin_183891729_17e8f1ce-af5e-462b-bc4a-08d4ebc7bb22-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/05/multimedia/05chauvin-trial-blog-arradondo/05chauvin-trial-blog-arradondo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/05/multimedia/05chauvin-trial-blog-arradondo/05chauvin-trial-blog-arradondo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/05/multimedia/05chauvin-trial-blog-arradondo/05chauvin-trial-blog-arradondo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What we know about Medaria Arradondo, the Minneapolis police chief.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Minneapolis’s Police Chief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'George Floyd Protests (2020)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arradondo, Medaria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-05T16:14:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marie Fazio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fazio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed10c887-f6a5-5046-831d-de942e6300b1', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed10c887-f6a5-5046-831d-de942e6300b1'}, {'abstract': 'An appeals court ruled that Andy Warhol violated a photographer’s copyright by appropriating her image for a silk-screen he did in 1984. Our critic disagrees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/05/arts/design/warhol-copyright-appeals-court.html', 'snippet': 'An appeals court ruled that Andy Warhol violated a photographer’s copyright by appropriating her image for a silk-screen he did in 1984. Our critic disagrees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few years back, a bevy of art critics declared that Marcel Duchamp’s 1917 sculpture called “Fountain” — a store-bought urinal he had presented, unchanged, as art — was the most influential work of the 20th century.  Andy Warhol’s 1964 Brillo Boxes — copies of scouring-pad cartons presented as art — could easily have come a close second. The philosopher Arthur Danto built an illustrious career, and a whole school of thought, around the importance of those boxes to understanding the very nature of artworks.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimed