ization': 'Reuters'}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/9258319e-a48f-56d6-92b3-ea2825adf5a9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/9258319e-a48f-56d6-92b3-ea2825adf5a9'}, {'abstract': 'His insights on global finance earned him a Nobel, while his more iconoclastic theories fostered the adoption of a single European currency and supply-side economics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/05/business/economy/robert-mundell-dead.html', 'snippet': 'His insights on global finance earned him a Nobel, while his more iconoclastic theories fostered the adoption of a single European currency and supply-side economics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robert A. Mundell, a Nobel Prize-winning economist whose theorizing opened the door to understanding the workings of global finance and the modern-day international economy, while his more iconoclastic views on economic policy fostered the creation of the euro and the adoption of the tax-cutting approach known as supply-side economics, died on Sunday at his home, a Renaissance-era palazzo that he and his wife restored, near Siena, Italy. He was 88.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/06/obituaries/03Mundell1-sub/03Mundell1-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/06/obituaries/03Mundell1-sub/03Mundell1-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/06/obituaries/03Mundell1-sub/03Mundell1-sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/06/obituaries/03Mundell1-sub/03Mundell1-sub-su