es.com/2021/04/06/magazine/how-to-apologize-to-a-child.html', 'snippet': 'Even if it’s difficult, admit you were wrong and share only your remorse.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We tell children, ‘Go apologize to your brother,’ but they can learn more by experiencing you apologizing to them,” says Jeremy Ruckstaetter, a professor of counseling at Covenant Theological Seminary in St. Louis, Mo. When Ruckstaetter started researching apologies in graduate school, he found perplexingly few studies focusing on apologies from parents to children. For his doctoral dissertation, he surveyed 327 parents and found that those who regularly apologized to their children reported stronger attachment bonds.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/11/magazine/11Mag-Tip-01/11Mag-Tip-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 580, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/11/magazine/11Mag-Tip-01/11Mag-Tip-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 580}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/11/magazine/11Mag-Tip-01/11Mag-Tip-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 990, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/11/magazine/11Mag-Tip-01/11Mag-Tip-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1981, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/11/magazine/11Mag-Tip-01/11Mag-Tip-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/11/magazine/11Mag-Tip-01/11Mag-Tip-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/11/magazine/11Mag-Tip-01/11Mag-Tip-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Apologize to a Child', 'kicker': 'Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Content Type: Service', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apologies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-06T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malia Wollan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wollan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5dc3ac6-443d-5170-a69c-d7304bca4fb3', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5dc3ac6-443d-5170-a69c-d7304bca4fb3'}, {'abstract': 'The conservative writer Helen Andrews and the liberal journalist Jill Filipovic discuss why millennials are so mad at their parents’ generation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/06/opinion/ezra-klein-podcast-helen-andrews-jill-filipovic-boomers.html', 'snippet': 'The conservative writer Helen Andrews and the liberal journalist Jill Filipovic discuss why millennials are so mad at their parents’ generation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald Trump was the fourth member of the baby boomer generation to be elected president, after Barack Obama, George W. Bush and Bill Clinton. The Senate majority leader, Chuck Schumer, is a boomer. Chief Justice John Roberts is a boomer. The Federal Reserve chair, Jerome Powell, is a boomer. President Joe Biden