h': 'JERUSALEM — Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu of Israel was asked by the president on Tuesday to try to form a new coalition government, offering a possible path for him to remain in office even as he stands trial on corruption charges.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/06/world/06israel-hfo-01/merlin_185467476_f99a8ad9-417c-4af7-b26e-ba9aef0a9156-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/06/world/06israel-hfo-01/merlin_185467476_f99a8ad9-417c-4af7-b26e-ba9aef0a9156-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 436}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/06/world/06israel-hfo-01/merlin_185467476_f99a8ad9-417c-4af7-b26e-ba9aef0a9156-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 744, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/06/world/06israel-hfo-01/merlin_185467476_f99a8ad9-417c-4af7-b26e-ba9aef0a9156-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1489, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/06/world/06israel-hfo-01/06israel-hfo-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/06/world/06israel-hfo-01/06israel-hfo-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/06/world/06israel-hfo-01/06israel-hfo-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge',