_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/06/world/asia/china-vaccination-drive.html', 'snippet': 'China’s Covid-19 vaccination campaign got off to a slow start. It is now trying to catch up, through a mixture of freebies and the occasional threat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Beijing, the vaccinated qualify for buy-one-get-one-free ice cream cones. In northern Gansu Province, a county government published a 20-stanza poem extolling the virtues of the jab. In the southern town of Wancheng, officials warned parents that if they refused to get vaccinated, their children’s schooling and future employment and housing were all at risk.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/06/world/06virus-china-vaccine-top/06virus-china-vaccine-top-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/06/world/06virus-china-vaccine-top/06virus-china-vaccine-top-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/06/world/06virus-china-vaccine-top/06virus-china-vaccine-top-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/06/world/06virus-china-vaccine-top/06virus-china-vaccine-top-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/06/world/06virus-china-vaccine-top/06virus-china-vaccine-top-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/06/world/06virus-china-vaccine-top/06virus-china-vaccine-top-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/06/world/06virus-china-vaccine-top/06virus-china-vaccine-top-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Will China Vaccinate 560 Million People? Start With Free Ice Cream.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Push 560 Million Doses? Try Free Ice Cream.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Propaganda', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gansu Province (China)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hainan Island (China)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chongqing (China)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-06T10:24:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian Wang and Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d666cab-597e-5a73-914b-8eecc98e3599', 'word_count': 1225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d666cab-597e-5a73-914b-8eecc98e3599'}, {'abstract': 'And now? Four million is the new benchmark for the U.S.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/06/briefing/three-million-daily-shots-achieved.html', 'snippet': 'And now? Four million is the new benchmark for the U.S.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shortly after President Biden took office, I began asking his aides why their publicly announced goal for Covid-19 vaccine distribution — an average of one million shots a day — was so unambitious. The pace wasn’t much faster than what the Trump administration had achieved in its final days, and it was far short of the rate at which vaccine makers would be delivering doses to the government. Based on that delivery schedule, a reasonable goal seemed to be three million shots a day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/06/lens/06ambriefing-promo/06ambriefing-vaccinations-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/06/lens/06ambriefing-promo/06ambriefing-vaccinations-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/06/lens/06ambriefing-promo/06ambriefing-vaccinations-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/06/lens/06ambriefing-promo/06ambriefing-vaccinations-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/