ed environments improve health) and ecotherapy (which considers the curative potential of natural settings).', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/05/t-magazine/forest-bathing-slide-1TWQ/forest-bathing-slide-1TWQ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/05/t-magazine/forest-bathing-slide-1TWQ/forest-bathing-slide-1TWQ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 436}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/05/t-magazine/forest-bathing-slide-1TWQ/forest-bathing-slide-1TWQ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 744, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/05/t-magazine/forest-bathing-slide-1TWQ/forest-bathing-slide-1TWQ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1488, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/05/t-magazine/forest-bathing-slide-1TWQ/forest-bathing-slide-1TWQ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/05/t-magazine/forest-bathing-slide-1TWQ/forest-bathing-slide-1TWQ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/05/t-magazine/forest-bathing-slide-1TWQ/forest-bathing-slide-1TWQ-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Create an At-Home Forest Bathing Ritual', 'kicker': 'On beauty', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Among the Trees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Perfumes and Fragrances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-06T19:17:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kari Molvar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Molvar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dddf46b8-8f0e-5646-b838-c9eb9f35c0b0', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dddf46b8-8f0e-5646-b838-c9eb9f35c0b0'}, {'abstract': 'If elite colleges are serious about diversity of class and race, there’s a simple solution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/06/opinion/stanford-admissions-campus.html', 'snippet': 'If elite colleges are serious about diversity of class and race, there’s a simple solution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stanford University’s faculty members may have convinced themselves that they struck a blow for egalitarianism when they voted for a policy meant to de-emphasize wealth in admitting undergraduates. But those professors should hold off on breaking out the champagne.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/06/opinion/06kirp/06kirp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/06/opinion/06kirp/06kirp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 60