may be easier than changing the Pentagon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/07/opinion/biden-defense-budget.html', 'snippet': 'President Biden wants to change the paradigm. That may be easier than changing the Pentagon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Biden loves spending money. Last month, he signed the $1.9 trillion American Rescue Plan to stimulate the economy. Now he’s pushing the $2 trillion American Jobs Plan to rebuild the nation’s infrastructure. He vows to follow that with the American Families Plan to improve health care, child care and education, which could cost billions or trillions more.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Let’s Cut Our Ridiculous Defense Budget', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense Contracts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Strategic and International Studies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for a New American Security', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Raytheon Company', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Northrop Grumman Corporation', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austin, Lloyd J III', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, William J', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-07T09:20:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Beinart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beinart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/18791653-b550-57ef-83af-4e6eb17c240f', 'word_count': 1058, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18791653-b550-57ef-83af-4e6eb17c240f'}, {'abstract': 'If Malcolm Gladwell is correct, Will Shortz is finally an expert.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/07/crosswords/crosswords-puzzles-shortz.html', 'snippet': 'If Malcolm Gladwell is correct, Will Shortz is finally an expert.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There may be only a handful of people in the puzzle community keeping track of such things, but on April 7, Will Shortz will have edited 10,000 puzzles since joining The New York Times as crossword editor in November 1993. That, of course, is an approximate number, counting from his start date. There are also the Variety puzzles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/07/crosswords/07wordplay-shortzportrait/07wordplay-shortzportrait-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/07/crosswords/07wordplay-shortzportrait/07wordplay-shortzportrait-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/07/crosswords/07wordplay-shortzportrait/07wordplay-shortzportrait-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/07/c