Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/309e39f4-cb9a-5278-98c3-66802eb197df', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/309e39f4-cb9a-5278-98c3-66802eb197df'}, {'abstract': 'The plan detailed by the Treasury Department would make it harder for companies to avoid paying taxes on both U.S. income and profits stashed abroad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/07/business/economy/biden-tax-plan.html', 'snippet': 'The plan detailed by the Treasury Department would make it harder for companies to avoid paying taxes on both U.S. income and profits stashed abroad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Large companies like Apple and Bristol Myers Squibb have long employed complicated maneuvers to reduce or eliminate their tax bills by shifting income on paper between countries. The strategy has enriched accountants and shareholders, while driving down corporate tax receipts for the federal government.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/07/business/07dc-biden-tax01alt/merlin_186090198_fcb3b1af-f41c-4516-bcd6-bf8abdde1883-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/07/business/07dc-biden-tax01alt/merlin_186090198_fcb3b1af-f41c-4516-bcd6-bf8abdde1883-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/07/business/07dc-biden-tax01alt/merlin_186090198_fcb3b1af-f41c-4516-bcd6-bf8abdde1883-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/07/business/07dc-biden-tax01alt/merlin_186090198_fcb3b1af-f41c-4516-bcd6-bf8abdde1883-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048