turn the mundane into memorable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You want Yusef Komunyakaa to write your poems for you. A Pulitzer Prize-winning poet, Komunyakaa has mastered the ability to turn the mundane into memorable. I remember reading this cat in prison wondering how he even conjured up the title “Neon Vernacular” or “Talking Dirty to the Gods.” His latest, “Everyday Mojo Songs of Earth,” gives us some classics. Like this one, “Ode to the Maggot.” The power is in recognizing, always, that the least of us matter. “Little/Master of earth, no one gets to heaven/Without going through you first.” Selected by Reginald Dwayne Betts', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/11/magazine/11mag-poem/11mag-poem-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/11/magazine/11mag-poem/11mag-poem-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/11/magazine/11mag-poem/11mag-poem-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 624, 'width': 918, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/11/magazine/11mag-poem/11mag-poem-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 624, 'width': 918, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/11/magazine/11mag-poem/11mag-poem-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/11/magazine/11mag-poem/11mag-poem-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0,