ernment forces and 89 civilians were killed in Afghanistan in April.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/08/world/asia/afghan-war-casualty-report-april-2021.html', 'snippet': 'At least 301 pro-government forces and 89 civilians were killed in Afghanistan in April.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At least 76 pro-government forces and 47 civilians were killed in Afghanistan the past week as the Taliban intensified their attacks across the country. The deadliest attack took place in Takhar Province, where a Taliban drone targeted a security outpost in the Chashma-e-Bangi area of Bangi district, killing seven pro-government militia members. In Wardak Province, seven civilians were killed in an airstrike by the Afghan air force in the Darawolang village of Jalrez district. Two children were among those killed. Afghan security forces started a clearing operation along the highway connecting Wardak to Kabul. During the operation, the Taliban fired on security forces from a house, which the air force later bombed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/29/world/29atwar-casualty-report/merlin_187058532_22ef1315-c4af-427a-8522-187e05874e0f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/29/world/29atwar-casualty-report/merlin_187058532_22ef1315-c4af-427a-8522-187e05874e0f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/29/world/29atwar-casualty-report/merlin_187058532_22ef1315-c4af-427a-8522-187e05874e0f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/29/world/29atwar-casualty-report/merlin_187058532_22