n American Jobs Plan, the economic theory that is Bidenomics is taking shape. It’s big. It puts climate at the center of everything. It is more worried about political risks — losing the House, giving Donald Trump a path back to power — than some traditional economic risks, like wasting money and bumping up inflation. It prefers to err on the side of spending more and making sure people know they got a bridge or a job than doing less and having people question whether government is working for them. But I still have a lot of questions about Bidenomics, in terms of both its economic theories and its political ones.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/09/opinion/09ekshow-deese-image/09ekshow-deese-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/09/opinion/09ekshow-deese-image/09ekshow-deese-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/09/opinion/09ekshow-deese-image/09ekshow-deese-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/09/opinion/09ekshow-deese-image/09ekshow-deese-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2047, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/09/opinion/09ekshow-deese-image/09ekshow-deese-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/09/opinion/09ekshow-deese-image/09ekshow-deese-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/09/opinion/09ekshow-deese-image/09ekshow-deese-image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Best Explanation of Biden’s Thinking I’ve Heard', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deese, Brian C (1978- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'American Jobs Plan (2021)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'American Rescue Plan (2021)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-09T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': "By ‘The Ezra Klein Show'", 'person': [], 'organization': "The Ezra Klein Show'"}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c58fa7c7-ecad-5623-ae43-5d2998ed6023', 'word_count': 7635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c58fa7c7-ecad-5623-ae43-5d2998ed6023'}, {'abstract': 'A budget that spends on education, homelessness and undocumented immigrants is the product of years of progressive politics, not a governor looking for a diversion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/09/nyregion/nyc-budget-taxing-rich.html', 'snippet': 'A budget that spends on education, homelessness and undocumented immigrants is the product of years of progressive politics, not a governor looking for a diversion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About a decade ago, it became increasingly common to hear public school parents in New York talk about carting rolls of paper t