'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e0c4149-09f6-551b-ae36-8ebb84f71097', 'word_count': 1354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e0c4149-09f6-551b-ae36-8ebb84f71097'}, {'abstract': 'Customers can start telling Jeff Bezos to treat his workers like human beings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/10/opinion/amazon-warehouse-workers-rights-unions.html', 'snippet': 'Customers can start telling Jeff Bezos to treat his workers like human beings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here are some of the ways that people who have worked inside Amazon’s warehouses describe the experience: “The job crushed my spirit and crippled my body.” “The lowest point in my life.” An “isolating colony of hell.” “They’re killing people mentally and physically.” “I began to hate my day-to-day life.” “The way Amazon pushes people is not moral.” “I had whole days where I didn’t talk to anyone.” “The systematic devaluing of human bodies.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/10/opinion/10manjoo-lead/10manjoo-lead-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/10/opinion/10manjoo-lead/10manjoo-lead-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/10/opinion/10manjoo-lead/10manjoo-lead-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/10/opinion/10manjoo-lead/10manjoo-lead-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'u