ganization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57761bb9-357b-56cc-b84c-3fd95888f9ed', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57761bb9-357b-56cc-b84c-3fd95888f9ed'}, {'abstract': 'With a little ingenuity, your sheet of newsprint can float safely to the ground.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/10/at-home/newspaper-parachute-activity.html', 'snippet': 'With a little ingenuity, your sheet of newsprint can float safely to the ground.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From Leonardo da Vinci’s pyramid design in the 15th century to the  supersonic version that helped land the Perseverance rover safely on Mars, the parachute, a device that catches air to control an object’s speed, has played an essential role in land, air, water and space travel. For all of the technology and resources that go into launching a spacecraft out of Earth’s atmosphere, it is the simple parachute that is key to safely landing it. A parachute’s canopy creates drag or air resistance, which means that the air below is pushed up against the underside of the canopy and slows its rate of descent.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/11/multimedia/11ah-parachute-activity/11ah-parachute-activity-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 749, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/11/multimedia/11ah-parachute-activity/11ah-parachute-activity-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 749}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/11/multimedia/11ah-parachute-activity/11ah-parachute-activity-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/11/mul