_id': 'nyt://article/de5df9fd-a323-524c-b6f0-ec28b738c0b9', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de5df9fd-a323-524c-b6f0-ec28b738c0b9'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections that appeared in print on Sunday, April 11, 2021.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/10/pageoneplus/corrections-april-11-2021.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections that appeared in print on Sunday, April 11, 2021.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An article this weekend on Page 7 about the impact of the pandemic on food pantries misstates the role of the National Guard in helping the Rev. Emaeyak Ekanem run a food pantry in the Bronx. Last year, the National Guard helped Mr. Ekanem set up his pantry for increased demand. It did not provide Mr. Ekanem with training before the pandemic, as he was never part of the National Guard.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: April 11, 2021', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-04-11T02:48:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ab6f324-a1be-58e3-b574-3166e750c754', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ab6f324-a1be-58e3-b574-3166e750c754'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Sunday, April 11, 2021.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/10/todayspaper/quotation-of-the-day-for-this-surge-whitmer-takes-hands-off-tack.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Sunday, April 11, 2021.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Policy change alone won’t change the tide. We need everyone to step up and to take personal responsibility here.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: For This Surge, Whitmer Takes Hands-Off Tack', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-04-11T02:50:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ecc9c10-f42d-5808-ba5a-fd73ae5e351e', 'word_count': 45, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ecc9c10-f42d-5808-ba5a-fd73ae5e351e'}, {'abstract': 'Is it possible that a sense of style is one more thing we lost during  the pandemic? Here’s why dressing to be seen in public seems so much harder now.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/10/at-home/virus-clothes.html', 'snippet': 'Is it possible that a sense of style is one more thing we lost during  the pandemic? Here’s why dressing to be seen in public seems so much harder now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Get-togethers are being planned without Zoom links. Restaurant diners are venturing back inside. As the vaccine rollout continues to gain speed, more companies are reopening their offices. We’re officially heading into new times. From a wardrobe perspective, these developments have generally meant one thing: putting on non-stretchy pants again.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/11/multimedia/11ah-closetillo/11ah-closetillo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 445, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/11/multimedia/11ah-closetillo/11ah-closetillo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 445}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/11/multimedia/11ah-closetillo/11ah-closetillo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 759, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', '