ad for the Exit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-04-12T00:14:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fe98d10-43f0-52d7-9f3a-c1c475ed4886', 'word_count': 38, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fe98d10-43f0-52d7-9f3a-c1c475ed4886'}, {'abstract': '“It’s going to be smart if people can continue to socially distance and wear masks,” Jerome Powell said on “60 Minutes.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/11/business/economy/jerome-powell-60-minutes.html', 'snippet': '“It’s going to be smart if people can continue to socially distance and wear masks,” Jerome Powell said on “60 Minutes.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The economy is at an “inflection point” and on the cusp of growing more quickly, the Federal Reserve chair, Jerome H. Powell, said in an interview broadcast on Sunday night. But he warned that the crisis was not yet over.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/13/business/11dc-powell-print/merlin_186173055_26237dbb-c42b-499b-9716-9b938ac80c29-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/13/business/11dc-powell-print/merlin_186173055_26237dbb-c42b-499b-9716-9b938ac80c29-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/13/business/11dc-powell-print/merlin_186173055_26237dbb-c42b-499b-9716-9b938ac80c29-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subt