large', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/08/opinion/08alter/08alter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 456, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/08/opinion/08alter/08alter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 456}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/08/opinion/08alter/08alter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 778, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/08/opinion/08alter/08alter-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1556, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/08/opinion/08alter/08alter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/08/opinion/08alter/08alter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/08/opinion/08alter/08alter-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How F.D.R.’s Heir Is Changing the Country', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roosevelt, Franklin Delano', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'American Jobs Plan (2021)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'American Rescue Plan (2021)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "New Deal (1930's)", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liberalism (US Politics)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-12T09:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Alter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e0c89be-b555-569c-991d-4fdfa0aa7788', 'word_count': 2063, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e0c89be-b555-569c-991d-4fdfa0aa7788'}, {'abstract': 'Christine Sun Kim: Growing up, I struggled to communicate and develop friendships with hearing peers, but then I went to college and became more comfortable with my signing and myself. Then I went to grad school, and my A.S.L. bubble popped. I learned I had a skill with strangers. I realized that small talk with hearing strangers was an opportunity for them to see me. And if I saw that they weren’t interested in me, I knew they weren’t worth my time, and it didn’t hurt my feelings — it was the filter I needed. Now when my friends and I are together, we communicate using a combination of American Sign Language (A.S.L.), German Sign Language (D.G.S.), international signs and [the messaging app] Cardzilla.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/12/t-magazine/sign-language-friends.html', 'snippet': '', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christine Sun Kim: Growing up, I struggled to communicate and develop friendships with hearing peers, but then I went to college and became more comfortable with my signing and myself. Then I went to grad school, and my A.S.L. bubble popped. I learned I had a skill with strangers. I realized that small talk with hearing strangers was an opportunity for them to see me. And if I saw that they weren’t interested in me, I knew they weren’t worth my time, and it didn’t hurt my feelings — it was the filter I needed. Now when my friends and I are together, we communicate using a combination of American Sign Language (A.S.L.), German Sign Language (D.G.S.), international signs and [the messaging app] Cardzilla.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '64', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-kimasl/12tmag-kimasl-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-kimasl/12tmag-kimasl-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-kimasl/12tmag-kimasl-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-kimasl/12tmag-kimasl-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1535, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-kimasl/12tmag-kimasl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-kimasl/12tmag-kimasl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-kimasl/12tmag-kimasl-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Friends Who Share a Language', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Friends Who Share a Language', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sign Language', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deafness', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim, Christine Sun', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-12T09:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gisela Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gisela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3711eab-af0c-5d6f-bb64-e87d83155848', 'word_count': 477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3711eab-af0c-5d6f-bb64-e87d83155848'}, {'abstract': 'The artist Ai Weiwei is inspired by the resilience and self-contentment of his beloved cats.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/12/t-magazine/ai-weiwei-cats.html', 'snippet': 'The artist Ai Weiwei is inspired by the resilience and self-contentment of his beloved cats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ai Weiwei: My cats think they are so important. They always want to sleep in the center of my bed or get on my shoulder, and I really have to negotiate with them. But they bring me so much joy. A neighbor found Shadow nearby, abandoned in some trash. She’s very small, but full of curiosity. Half is 6, and more sophisticated — I brought him with me to Portugal from my studio in Berlin, where I lived between 2015 and 2020 — and Yellow was a local street cat I took in. He’s very attached to humans. If I go on a walk, he follows me, almost like a dog. But of course, all cats are independent, and our house here is in the middle of a field, so they can run around all day. In Berlin, we were on an upper floor of an apartment building, and Half and another cat I had then jumped out of a window. Fortunately, they weren’t hurt. Cats are so capable. It’s amazing. Any other animal would be dead.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '83', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-weiwei-slide-FZAK-copy/12tmag-weiwei-slide-FZAK-copy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 608, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-weiwei-slide-FZAK-copy/12tmag-weiwei-slide-FZAK-copy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 608}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-weiwei-slide-FZAK-copy/12tmag-weiwei-slide-FZAK-copy-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1012, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-weiwei-slide-FZAK-copy/12tmag-weiwei-slide-FZAK-copy-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2023, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-weiwei-slide-FZAK-copy/12tmag-weiwei-slide-FZAK-copy-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-weiwei-slide-FZAK-copy/12tmag-weiwei-slide-FZAK-copy-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-weiwei-slide-FZAK-copy/12tmag-weiwei-slide-FZAK-copy-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Furry Friends', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Furry Friends', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cats', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ai Weiwei', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-12T09:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alice Newell-Hanson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newell-Hanson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4c59ea2-bb46-5abc-a5eb-88bacce6f99c', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4c59ea2-bb46-5abc-a5eb-88bacce6f99c'}, {'abstract': 'For this creative group, the Pines remains a summer haven for queerness and connection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/12/t-magazine/fire-island-pines-artists.html', 'snippet': 'For this creative group, the Pines remains a summer haven for queerness and connection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'T.M. Davy: Our first summer out here was in 2012, thanks to a nonprofit called Boffo, started by Faris Al-Shathir, which runs an artists’ residency I participated in. A group of us have been coming to Fire Island ever since — we’ve become like family. Queer artists have spent time in the Pines for decades: The group PaJaMa — Paul Cadmus and Jared and Margaret French — were here in the 1930s, getting weird. It’s just right for the light and for the ocean and for getting away from other people’s eyes. David Hockney was playing in the Pines in the 1970s, before AIDS devastated the creative community.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '62', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-davyeisenman/12tmag-davyeisenman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-davyeisenman/12tmag-davyeisenman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-davyeisenman/12tmag-davyeisenman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-davyeisenman/12tmag-davyeisenman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-davyeisenman/12tmag-davyeisenman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-davyeisenman/12tmag-davyeisenman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-davyeisenman/12tmag-davyeisenman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Friends', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weekend Friends', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fire Island (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eisenman, Nicole', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-12T09:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jameson Fitzpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jameson', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fitzpatrick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5895f3a6-b7e6-5167-adcf-c5b81173e557', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5895f3a6-b7e6-5167-adcf-c5b81173e557'}, {'abstract': 'For the floral designer Louis-Géraud Castor, creating a bouquet for someone is inherently personal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/12/t-magazine/louis-geraud-castor-florist-paris.html', 'snippet': 'For the floral designer Louis-Géraud Castor, creating a bouquet for someone is inherently personal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Louis-Géraud Castor: I have always loved flowers, so about four years ago, I left a 15-year career as an art dealer to attend the École des Fleuristes de Paris. Since I opened my studio in 2017, I have grown a little community, a village of people, really, and what we have in common is a respect for the beauty of the flower.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '78', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-castor-slide-0RFX-copy/12tmag-castor-slide-0RFX-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-castor-slide-0RFX-copy/12tmag-castor-slide-0RFX-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-castor-slide-0RFX-copy/12tmag-castor-slide-0RFX-copy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-castor-slide-0RFX-copy/12tmag-castor-slide-0RFX-copy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-castor-slide-0RFX-copy/12tmag-castor-slide-0RFX-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-castor-slide-0RFX-copy/12tmag-castor-slide-0RFX-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-castor-slide-0RFX-copy/12tmag-castor-slide-0RFX-copy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clients Who Became Friends', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clients Who Became Friends', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Florists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-12T09:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Wilkinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilkinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4287867b-5675-5a18-a6a1-63f3938cfe72', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4287867b-5675-5a18-a6a1-63f3938cfe72'}, {'abstract': 'For Linux, Xunami Muse, Bobby LeMaire and the rest of their close-knit group, finding your chosen family means never having to be alone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/12/t-magazine/queer-nightlife-chosen-family.html', 'snippet': 'For Linux, Xunami Muse, Bobby LeMaire and the rest of their close-knit group, finding your chosen family means never having to be alone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Linux: I really hope that we live to be old, old, old ladies one day — no one is dying on us young. I hope we’re the oldest women to live in the history of old-age women. And when we look back at our 20s, I hope that we think, “Oh, honey, that was just the beginning! I can’t believe we used to be that poor, and that we used to struggle like that.” When we look around at each other much later, we’ll have lived a full life and have experienced so many things — been onstage for millions of people, been pop stars, flown on private jets, lived the life. I hope all of our dreams manifest and materialize themselves. We’re getting interviewed by The New York Times now, but when we look back, I hope we think that these were our struggle days. It’s only the beginning.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '84', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-transclubkids/12tmag-transclubkids-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-transclubkids/12tmag-transclubkids-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-transclubkids/12tmag-transclubkids-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-transclubkids/12tmag-transclubkids-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-transclubkids/12tmag-transclubkids-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-transclubkids/12tmag-transclubkids-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-transclubkids/12tmag-transclubkids-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Friends Who Protect One Another', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Friends Who Protect One Another', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexuals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-12T09:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Río Sofia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Río', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sofia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/710cc542-efc0-5d9b-9e08-9954aef5b96e', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/710cc542-efc0-5d9b-9e08-9954aef5b96e'}, {'abstract': 'Michelle A. Williams, an epidemiologist and Harvard dean, urges politicians to focus on public health if they want a strong economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/12/opinion/sway-kara-swisher-michelle-williams.html', 'snippet': 'Michelle A. Williams, an epidemiologist and Harvard dean, urges politicians to focus on public health if they want a strong economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'States have experimented with vastly differing responses to the coronavirus pandemic — from Gov. Andrew Cuomo’s strict lockdown in New York to Gov. Ron DeSantis’s resistance to a mask mandate in Florida. In defending their choices, leaders have often cited a trade-off between the economy and public health. But Michelle A. Williams, an epidemiologist and dean of Harvard’s T.H. Chan School of Public Health, says those two factors don’t have to be in conflict. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subt