N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard School of Public Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Michelle A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus Reopenings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disease Rates', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeSantis, Ron', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-12T09:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': "By ‘Sway'", 'person': [{'firstname': "Sway'", 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/50fab1ce-2aaa-59bb-ab3c-3aa797f34d5a', 'word_count': 208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50fab1ce-2aaa-59bb-ab3c-3aa797f34d5a'}, {'abstract': 'For each person who dies of Covid-19, experts say there are at least nine newly bereaved. We must begin to address the toll.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/12/opinion/covid-death-grief.html', 'snippet': 'For each person who dies of Covid-19, experts say there are at least nine newly bereaved. We must begin to address the toll.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The end of the Covid-19 crisis in the United States is in sight, thanks to effective vaccines being deployed on a massive scale. But the still growing death toll will leave behind millions of bereaved people, wracked by the suffering that the loss of a loved one can bring. This is a public health crisis with consequences that may last generations, which we do not currently have the policy tools or resources to address.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/opinio