 Just Do What You Were Told?” collects a few dozen of Diski’s best pieces for the London Review of Books.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Herman Tarnower, the murdered diet-book writer, tried to class up his offices in Scarsdale by strewing them with British publications. It didn’t seem to have worked.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/14/books/review/13BOOKDISKI1/13BOOKDISKI1-articleLarge.png', 'height': 884, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/14/books/review/13BOOKDISKI1/13BOOKDISKI1-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 884}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/14/books/review/13BOOKDISKI1/13BOOKDISKI1-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 696, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/14/books/review/13BOOKDISKI1/13BOOKDISKI1-superJumbo.png', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1391, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/14/books/review/13BOOKDISKI1/13BOOKDISKI1-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/14/books/review/13BOOKDISKI1/13BOOKDISKI1-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/14/books/review/13BOOKDISKI1/13BOOKDISKI1-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Prime Cuts From Jenny Diski’s Catalog of Intimate, Witty Essays', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Room With Smoke, Coffee and Her Words', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Why Didn't You Just Do What You Were Told?: Essays (Book)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diski, Jenny', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-12T09:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/eca2a11c-b4d3-58d6-a112-a233bcc0e9ab', 'word_count': 1025, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eca2a11c-b4d3-58d6-a112-a233bcc0e9ab'}, {'abstract': '“This crisis affects more or less everyone, and poetry can help us process difficult feelings like loss, sadness, anger, lack of hope.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/12/well/mind/national-poetry-month-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': '“This crisis affects more or less everyone, and poetry can help us process difficult feelings like loss, sadness, anger, lack of hope.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many, perhaps most, of us have spent this past year struggling to find ways to mourn the losses, weather the stresses and revive the pleasures stolen by the Covid-19 pandemic. We’ve monitored Zoom funerals, weddings, graduations, christenings, bar and bat mitzvahs, alternately laughing and weeping at inanimate screens as we tried to make sense of a world turned upside down.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/science/12SCI-B