turepromo-jumbo.gif', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-culturepromo/12tmag-culturepromo-superJumbo.gif', 'height': 720, 'width': 1080, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-culturepromo/12tmag-culturepromo-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-culturepromo/12tmag-culturepromo-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-culturepromo/12tmag-culturepromo-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Celebration of Friendship in All Its Many Forms', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-12T09:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/5bae4697-628f-5356-bccf-d7afba391079', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/5bae4697-628f-5356-bccf-d7afba391079'}, {'abstract': 'An artist and a writer who, despite being at different stages of their lives, have forged a deep bond.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/12/t-magazine/nan-goldin-thora-siemsen.html', 'snippet': 'An artist and a writer who, despite being at different stages of their lives, have forged a deep bond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thora Siemsen: We met in December 2019 at Saluggi’s in TriBeCa, when I interviewed Nan about the reissue of her 1993 book “The Other Side” and her last show at Marian Goodman Gallery in London. We talked for hours. I flew home to Colorado the next day for the holidays and, when I got back to New York, we picked up where we’d left off. We started playing backgammon and began what I refer to as “film school,” where Nan teaches me about movies — we started with Hitchcock and Visconti, and everything starring Judy Holliday and Barbara Stanwyck. When we heard about the impending lockdown, we had a conversation about what it would look like to quarantine together. I made the decision to move into her home in Clinton Hill quickly, but it was the right one. I feel like myself with Nan: like an adult, safe. For her birthday last September, I took her to Holy Land U.S.A., this run-down religious theme park in Connecticut that was in one of our favorite movies, “Wanda” (1970). This past summer, I went swimming for the first time since going on hormones. From a boat, Nan took a picture that is precious to me. Her photographs allow me to replay those moments when I felt beautiful.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '71', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-goldinsiemsen-copy/12tmag-goldinsiemsen-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-goldinsiemsen-copy/12tmag-goldinsiemsen-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-goldinsiemsen-copy/12tmag-goldinsiemsen-copy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-goldinsiemsen-copy/12tmag-goldinsiemsen-copy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-goldinsiemsen-copy/12tmag-goldinsiemsen-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-goldinsiemsen-copy/12tmag-goldinsiemsen-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-goldinsiemsen-copy/12tmag-goldinsiemsen-copy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Friends Who Teach Each Other', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Friends Who Teach Each Other', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldin, Nan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Backgammon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-12T09:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Coco Romack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Coco', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_mat