51, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4835a8b-7b5c-5848-9b6e-2b6fc46af52d'}, {'abstract': 'For the creative director Anthony Vaccarello, two icons of French style inform how he approaches every collection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/12/t-magazine/yves-saint-laurent-muses.html', 'snippet': 'For the creative director Anthony Vaccarello, two icons of French style inform how he approaches every collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anthony Vaccarello: For me, Catherine and Betty are the epitome of Saint Laurent style. They are the last ones with testimonies of who the real Yves Saint Laurent was. Each season, they are the only people whose opinions mean anything to me.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '58', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-vaccarello/12tmag-vaccarello-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-vaccarello/12tmag-vaccarello-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-vaccarello/12tmag-vaccarello-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 620, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-vaccarello/12tmag-vaccarello-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1239, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-vaccarello/12tmag-vaccarello-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-vaccarello/12tmag-vaccarello-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-vaccarello/12tmag-vaccarello-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Friends Who Are Muses', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Friends Who Are Muses', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vaccarello, Anthony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deneuve, Catherine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yves Saint Laurent', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-12T09:02:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noor Brara', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brara', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74899c42-7aa7-5994-abd9-3230d81eccfc', 'word_count': 670, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74899c42-7aa7-5994-abd9-3230d81eccfc'}, {'abstract': 'Though they started off as teacher and student, Catherine Opie and Sam Richardson have forged a bond that transcends institutional hierarchies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/12/t-magazine/catherine-opie-sam-richardson.html', 'snippet': 'Though they started off as teacher and student, Catherine Opie and Sam Richardson have forged a bond that transcends institutional hierarchies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Catherine Opie: I met Sam over a series of phone calls in 2018 when she was considering U.C.L.A. for grad school. I was the head of the photography program, and there were only three spots. When I look at a potential student’s work, I want to see that they’re having a conversation with ideas, and with the history of photography. Hopefully, I can be another voice in that conversation.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '88', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-opierichardson/12tmag-opierichardson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-opierichardson/12tmag-opierichardson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 451}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-opierichardson/12tmag-opierichardson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-opierichardson/12tmag-opierichardson-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1539, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-opierichardson/12tmag-opierichardson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-opierichardson/12tmag-opierichardson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-opierichardson/12tmag-opierichardson-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mentor/Protégée Friends', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mentor/Protégée Friends', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Opie, Catherine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-12T09:02:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kerry Manders', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Manders', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a5ce2bf-a95b-5338-bc71-0ba4c8c4ddde', 'word_count': 628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a5ce2bf-a95b-5338-bc71-0ba4c8c4ddde'}, {'abstract': 'In an unusual season, a director and some of his closest collaborators came together on the Sicilian coast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/12/t-magazine/luca-guadagnino-italy-summer.html', 'snippet': 'In an unusual season, a director and some of his closest collaborators came together on the Sicilian coast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Luca Guadagnino: I spent the entirety of the first lockdown from March onward with my pal the photographer Alessio Bolzoni, whom I also work with on my films, and then in June, after restrictions in Italy started to ease, I was asked to do a campaign for Ferragamo in Milan. I called my very dear friend Fernanda Pérez — a makeup artist whom I’ve worked with since my first film, “The Protagonists” (1999) — to see if she wanted to join Alessio and me for the project. I live there, and she lives in Buenos Aires. She flew in with her now-13-year-old daughter, Frida, whom I’ve known since she was a baby; I held her in my lap when we were filming “I Am Love” (2009).', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '66', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-guadagnino-slide-BOI8-copy/12tmag-guadagnino-slide-BOI8-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-guadagnino-slide-BOI8-copy/12tmag-guadagnino-slide-BOI8-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-guadagnino-slide-BOI8-copy/12tmag-guadagnino-slide-BOI8-copy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-guadagnino-slide-BOI8-copy/12tmag-guadagnino-slide-BOI8-copy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1314, 'width': 1971, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-guadagnino-slide-BOI8-copy/12tmag-guadagnino-slide-BOI8-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-guadagnino-slide-BOI8-copy/12tmag-guadagnino-slide-BOI8-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-guadagnino-slide-BOI8-copy/12tmag-guadagnino-slide-BOI8-copy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Friends Who Summer Together', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Friends Who Summer Together', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guadagnino, Luca', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sicily (Italy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Palermo (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-12T09:02:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noor Brara', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brara', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c021f56e-ca9a-5542-9772-6ed083eb3dd8', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c021f56e-ca9a-5542-9772-6ed083eb3dd8'}, {'abstract': 'A look back at one of those relationships where, despite changes in circumstance and place, two people are able to pick up where they left off.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/12/t-magazine/long-distance-friends.html', 'snippet': 'A look back at one of those relationships where, despite changes in circumstance and place, two people are able to pick up where they left off.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I MET REI at an artists’ residency in the late 2000s, when the New England landscape was at its greenest and most vertiginous. At dusk, wood thrushes chimed their watery, ethereal songs, which I now associate with freedom and creative ferment. I recall Rei entering the screened-in porch where a few residents were smoking and introducing himself as a composer from Japan. He was 32, about the same age I was at the time, and wore a baggy black hoodie, trousers and thick, white-framed glasses. He kept his hair longer in the front so that a thicket of bangs swept just past his left eyebrow. He was tall, and if you looked closely, he was attractive. But it was hard to notice that because he was quiet and looked as if he wanted to shrink into himself, like a teenage boy who’d shot up over the span of the summer.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '44', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-essays-slide-VQAG-copy/12tmag-essays-slide-VQAG-copy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-essays-slide-VQAG-copy/12tmag-essays-slide-VQAG-copy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-essays-slide-VQAG-copy/12tmag-essays-slide-VQAG-copy-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-essays-slide-VQAG-copy/12tmag-essays-slide-VQAG-copy-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1206, 'width': 1808, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-essays-slide-VQAG-copy/12tmag-essays-slide-VQAG-copy-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-essays-slide-VQAG-copy/12tmag-essays-slide-VQAG-copy-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-essays-slide-VQAG-copy/12tmag-essays-slide-VQAG-copy-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Composer of Noise', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Long-Distance Friends', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fukushima (Japan)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-12T09:02:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Park Hong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': 'Park', 'lastname': 'Hong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2562ee52-2975-5ee7-a8e0-52122673c6d5', 'word_count': 2186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2562ee52-2975-5ee7-a8e0-52122673c6d5'}, {'abstract': "Whether in Seoul or New York, this trio of Korean models feel at home when they're together.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/12/t-magazine/korean-models-hometown-friends.html', 'snippet': "Whether in Seoul or New York, this trio of Korean models feel at home when they're together.", 'lead_paragraph': 'Sohyun Jung: My first New York Fashion Week, I was 21 and still didn’t speak English very well. I was doing a fitting for Marc Jacobs’s fall 2017 runway show, and couldn’t understand what anyone was saying and why I was waiting around for three hours. It was nothing like Seoul Fashion Week. My phone died. I started to panic. But then, another Korean model approached me and comforted me. She invited me to sit with her and let me borrow her phone charger. She translated the announcements and told me when it was my turn to be fitted. That woman was HoYeon Jung — she was a year older than I was, and it was her third New York Fashion Week. In Korean culture, we take care of each other, especially when we’re working overseas. We commute to fittings and eat together between shows. I met EZ six years ago at a party in Seoul, and when we went to New York for fashion week, we lived together for the whole season and got really close. I met Chloe recently in New York, but I already consider her a younger sister. What I’ve longed for over the past year has been that sense of community, of going out in Seoul with EZ and my other model friends, like Sora Choi and Yoon Young Bae. We’d meet in Gangnam, where most of us live, and from there we’d have dinner — usually street food, like tteokbokki [a spicy rice cake], dakbal [spicy chicken feet] or Korean barbecue — then bowling, karaoke and bar hopping until we’d end up at one of our apartments to play drinking games and card games, like Go Stop. I’d often end up going home when people were heading to work. I really miss those days.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '87', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-koreanmodels-slide-6KTR-copy/12tmag-koreanmodels-slide-6KTR-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-koreanmodels-slide-6KTR-copy/12tmag-koreanmodels-slide-6KTR-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-koreanmodels-slide-6KTR-copy/12tmag-koreanmodels-slide-6KTR-copy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-koreanmodels-slide-6KTR-copy/12tmag-koreanmodels-slide-6KTR-copy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1269, 'width': 1904, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-koreanmodels-slide-6KTR-copy/12tmag-koreanmodels-slide-6KTR-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-koreanmodels-slide-6KTR-copy/12tmag-koreanmodels-slide-6KTR-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-koreanmodels-slide-6KTR-copy/12tmag-koreanmodels-slide-6KTR-copy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hometown Friends', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hometown Friends', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Korean Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-12T09:02:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Angela Koh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Angela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Koh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c1ba3e4-ab09-5532-b1bd-7f9f320a4fcb', 'word_count': 504, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c1ba3e4-ab09-5532-b1bd-7f9f320a4fcb'}, {'abstract': 'For this multigenerational crew of artists, curators and a musician, kinship and collaboration go hand in hand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/12/t-magazine/hank-willis-thomas-family.html', 'snippet': 'For this multigenerational crew of artists, curators and a musician, kinship and collaboration go hand in hand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Deborah Willis: This year, it was important for me to think about lockdown as a framework, and also what it meant at the heart of it: having a 2-year-old granddaughter I couldn’t see and a 98-year-old mother I couldn’t visit. Hank, Ru and I are not only family but friends. Our relationship as collaborators began at the kitchen table, where we discussed shared experiences about representation, and it continues there.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '61', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-willisthomas/12tmag-willisthomas-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-willisthomas/12tmag-willisthomas-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-willisthomas/12tmag-willisthomas-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 