eywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALMODOVAR, PEDRO', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Penelope', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Banderas, Antonio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Actors and Actresses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Palma, Rossy (1964- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Content Type: Personal Profile', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-12T09:02:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Snyder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Snyder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c35d449-d120-531c-91ac-44ca2523ed44', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c35d449-d120-531c-91ac-44ca2523ed44'}, {'abstract': 'With good friends, as with great art, our sense of the world is challenged and transformed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/12/t-magazine/friendship-art-creative-partnerships.html', 'snippet': 'With good friends, as with great art, our sense of the world is challenged and transformed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STORIES OF FRIENDSHIPS between artists are often told as love stories: the chance meeting, the electric first encounter, the mysterious mutual recognition that would change everything. That summer day in 1967 when Robert Mapplethorpe ran into Patti Smith in a New York City bookstore, both 20-year-olds craving beauty and immortality — “I thought to myself that he contained an entire universe I just had to know,” Smith wrote in her 2010 memoir, “Just Kids.” The afternoon in 1940 when a teenage James Baldwin knocked on the door of Beauford Delaney’s Greenwich Village studio (“the first walking, living proof, for me, that a Black man could be an artist,” Baldwin wrote in his 1985 essay “The Price of a Ticket” of meeting the painter). But lightning doesn’t always strike on initial acquaintance. In a 1917 diary entry, a 35-year-old Virginia Woolf didn’t mince words in her impression of the New Zealand-born Modernist writer Katherine Mansfield at a dinner party: “She stinks like a … civet cat that had taken to streetwalking.” Despite Mansfield’s shocking “commonness,” Woolf went on, “when this diminishes, she is so intelligent and inscrutable that she repays friendship.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '35', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-onfriendship-slide-DNCZ/12tmag-onfriendship-slide-DNCZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 349, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-onfriendship-slide-DNCZ/12tmag-onfriendship-slide-DNCZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 349}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-onfriendship-slide-DNCZ/12tmag-onfriendship-slide-DNCZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 596, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-onfriendship-slide-DNCZ/12tmag-onfriendship-slide-DNCZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1193, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/t-magazine/12tmag-onfriendship-slide-DNCZ/12tmag-onfriendship-slide-DNCZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'heig