day, after an officer fatally shot a 20-year-old Black driver during a traffic stop. The shooting occurred not far from the courthouse where Derek Chauvin is on trial for the death of George Floyd.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Business owners assess the damage after a night of unrest outside Minneapolis.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-04-12T21:51:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef90340b-10d2-5c86-8d9b-ddb85b7f16fb', 'word_count': 59, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef90340b-10d2-5c86-8d9b-ddb85b7f16fb'}, {'abstract': 'The governor outlined how schools and colleges may hold commencement ceremonies in the coming months, with curtailed attendance tied to the capacity of venues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/12/world/new-york-graduation-ceremonies.html', 'snippet': 'The governor outlined how schools and colleges may hold commencement ceremonies in the coming months, with curtailed attendance tied to the capacity of venues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Schools and colleges across New York State will be allowed to hold graduation ceremonies for students this spring, with restrictions depending on type of venue or its capacity, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo said on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/world/12virus-briefing-nygraduation1/12virus-briefing-nygraduation1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/12/world/12virus-briefing-nygraduation1/12virus-briefing-nygraduation1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0