ations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-13T16:16:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pam Belluck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belluck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a732acc-6011-5de7-ab17-7c210d68268a', 'word_count': 562, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a732acc-6011-5de7-ab17-7c210d68268a'}, {'abstract': 'If confirmed to oversee the U.S. Agency for International Development, Samantha Power will confront adversaries by bolstering democracy and human rights. China is an early focus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/13/us/politics/samantha-power-biden.html', 'snippet': 'If confirmed to oversee the U.S. Agency for International Development, Samantha Power will confront adversaries by bolstering democracy and human rights. China is an early focus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Near the end of the 2014 documentary “Watchers of the Sky,” which chronicles the origins of the legal definition of genocide, Samantha Power grows emotional. At the time, Ms. Power was President Barack Obama’s ambassador to the United Nations, and, she said, had “great visibility into a lot of the pain” in the world.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/12/us/politics/12dc-power1/merlin_185444808_59bdd490-35bd-4461-bd72-72a832c36088-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/12/us/politics/12dc-power1/merlin_185444808_59bdd490-35bd-4461-bd72-72a832c36088-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'capt