None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/25/books/review/Freeberg/Freeberg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/25/books/review/Freeberg/Freeberg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/25/books/review/Freeberg/Freeberg-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Long History of Those Who Fought to Save the Animals', 'kicker': 'Nonfiction', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Endangered', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wildlife Trade and Poaching', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservation of Resources', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biodiversity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nijhuis, Michelle', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Beloved Beasts: Fighting for Life in an Age of Extinction (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-14T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ernest Freeberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ernest', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Freeberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a12fdd58-d8bc-555a-8df0-8d285beb86f4', 'word_count': 1246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a12fdd58-d8bc-555a-8df0-8d285beb86f4'}, {'abstract': 'Ross Douthat and Michelle Goldberg return to the podcast to debate the future of abortion in America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/14/opinion/abortion-roe-douthat-goldberg.html', 'snippet': 'Ross Douthat and Michelle Goldberg return to the podcast to debate the future of abortion in America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court — and its post-Donald Trump conservative majority — is currently deciding whether to take up a case that could be the final blow to Roe v. Wade. Overturning Roe, the 48-year-old decision protecting the right to an abortion in America, would leave abortion regulation up to the states. But some abortion opponents think that’s not far enough and are pushing the movement to change its focus to securing a 14th Amendment declaration of fetal personhood.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why the Anti-Abortion Side Will Lose, Even if It Wins', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Abortion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'First Things (Magazine)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finnis, John (1940- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-14T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': "By ‘The Argument'", 'person': [], 'organization': "The Argument'"}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa05d885-fc78-5b98-b32c-d3c6e16850de', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa05d885-fc78-5b98-b32c-d3c6e16850de'}, {'abstract': 'The idea that regulation chills activity in new markets is intuitive, but not always accurate. Sometimes the opposite is true.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/14/opinion/coinbase-ipo-cryptocurrencies.html', 'snippet': 'The idea that regulation chills activity in new markets is intuitive, but not always accurate. Sometimes the opposite is true.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since last fall, cryptocurrencies — digital tokens that represent monetary value, stored on completely decentralized networks of public digital ledgers — have boomed. It’s led to a bullish frenzy among those who see them as a generational wealth-creation opportunity or view themselves as the eventual survivors of an inflation-driven collapse of traditional currencies like the U.S. dollar.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/14/opinion/14feinsteinwerbach/14feinsteinwerbach-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/14/opinion/14feinsteinwerbach/14feinsteinwerbach-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/14/opinion/14feinsteinwerbach/14feinsteinwerbach-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/14/opinion/14feinsteinwerbach/14feinsteinwerbach-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/14/opinion/14feinsteinwerbach/14feinsteinwerbach-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/14/opinion/14feinsteinwerbach/14feinsteinwerbach-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/14/opinion/14feinsteinwerbach/14feinsteinwerbach-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Fear Cryptocurrencies. Manage Them.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Virtual Currency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coinbase Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bitcoin (Currency)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-14T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Feinstein and Kevin Werbach', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feinstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werbach', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/47790648-0bbd-53bf-9f14-4017216f36ef', 'word_count': 1011, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47790648-0bbd-53bf-9f14-4017216f36ef'}, {'abstract': 'The Ethical Society of Police isn’t afraid to speak out against police misconduct.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/14/opinion/police-officer-unions.html', 'snippet': 'The Ethical Society of Police isn’t afraid to speak out against police misconduct.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, a veteran officer in Brooklyn Center, Minn., killed an unarmed man, claiming to have mistaken her gun for her Taser. The Ethical Society of Police, a St. Louis group consisting mostly of Black officers, was quick to comment on the shooting, calling out the negligence of the officer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I’m in a Police Union That Holds Bad Cops Accountable', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'George Floyd Protests (2020)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Lives Matter Movement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics and Official Misconduct', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'St Louis (Mo)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-14T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cheryl E. Orange', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cheryl', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Orange', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1cdba6e-cbd4-578e-864e-fcc63f96fb6a', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1cdba6e-cbd4-578e-864e-fcc63f96fb6a'}, {'abstract': 'The Times wants to see families finally welcoming new babies that they couldn’t see in person during the pandemic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/14/parenting/pandemic-baby-meet-family.html', 'snippet': 'The Times wants to see families finally welcoming new babies that they couldn’t see in person during the pandemic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An overjoyed grandmother cradling the baby she’s only seen over FaceTime. An uncle crying openly with relief when he finally meets his new nephew. The cluster of sweet young cousins greeting the smallest member of their family for the first time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/23/well/23par-awkward-reunions/23par-awkward-reunions-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/23/well/23par-awkward-reunions/23par-awkward-reunions-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/23/well/23par-awkward-reunions/23par-awkward-reunions-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/23/well/23par-awkward-reunions/23par-awkward-reunions-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1166, 'width': 1750, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/23/well/23par-awkward-reunions/23par-awkward-reunions-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/23/well/23par-awkward-reunions/23par-awkward-reunions-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/23/well/23par-awkward-reunions/23par-awkward-reunions-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Show Us Your Pandemic Baby Family Reunions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus Reopenings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grandparents', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-14T09:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Parenting', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b447d616-1157-5efa-8519-417106b007c9', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b447d616-1157-5efa-8519-417106b007c9'}, {'abstract': 'With some trepidation, Gabrielle Hamilton puts her own spin on risi e bisi — rice and peas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/14/magazine/venetian-rice-and-peas-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'With some trepidation, Gabrielle Hamilton puts her own spin on risi e bisi — rice and peas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a joke going around that divorce lawyers are limbering up for the post-\u200bpandemic onslaught of work headed their way. If you’ve ever had your marriage fall apart, it’s not the funniest joke, especially when there are kids involved. But here’s a really funny one in the opposite direction: The pandemic dissolved all residual rancor and friction between me and my ex-husband as soon as New York City shut down. Our situation created the urgent, nonnegotiable necessity for smooth cooperation: We have two children, and they had to go back and forth between our homes. No one could be harmed in the shuffle.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/18/magazine/18mag-eat/18mag-eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/18/magazine/18mag-eat/18mag-eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 451}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/18/magazine/18mag-eat/18mag-eat-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 770, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/18/magazine/18mag-eat/18mag-eat-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1541, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/18/magazine/18mag-eat/18mag-eat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/18/magazine/18mag-eat/18mag-eat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/18/magazine/18mag-eat/18mag-eat-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Classic Venetian Dish That Doesn’t Need Improvement', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Authentically Spring', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegetables', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Peas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zucchini', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-14T09:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gabrielle Hamilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabrielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hamilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bea6e70-36aa-59f8-9cd6-9eefe4952619', 'word_count': 931, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bea6e70-36aa-59f8-9cd6-9eefe4952619'}, {'abstract': 'It felt like the itch was coming from somehow under her skin. The cause ended up being even deeper.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/14/magazine/hodgkin-lymphoma-diagnosis.html', 'snippet': 'It felt like the itch was coming from somehow under her skin. The cause ended up being even deeper.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was dark by the time the 41-year-old woman was able to start the long drive from her father’s apartment in Washington, D.C., to her home in Westchester County, N.Y. She was eager to get back to her husband and three children. Somewhere after she crossed the border into Maryland, the woman suddenly developed a terrible itch all over her body. She’d been a little itchy for the past couple of weeks but attributed that to dry skin from her now-faded summertime tan. This seemed very different: much stronger, much deeper. And absolutely everywhere, all at the same time.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/18/magazine/18Mag-Diagnosis-1/18Mag-Diagnosis-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 466, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/18/magazine/18Mag-Diagnosis-1/18Mag-Diagnosis-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 466}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumb