afghanistan-war-biden-veterans.html', 'snippet': 'It’s not guilt, shame or regret I feel. It’s the sense of having done a terrible duty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When President Biden announced on Wednesday that the United States would withdraw all its troops from Afghanistan by Sept. 11, 2021, he appeared to be finally bringing this “forever war” to an end. Although I have waited for this moment for a decade, it is impossible to feel relief. The Sept. 11 attacks took place during my senior year of college, and the wars in Iraq and Afghanistan that followed consumed the entirety of my adult life. Although history books may mark this as the end of the Afghanistan war, it will never be over for many of my generation who fought.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/18/opinion/14kudo2/14kudo2-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/18/opinion/14kudo2/14kudo2-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/18/opinion/14kudo2/14kudo2-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/18/opinion/14kudo2/14kudo2-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/18/opinion/14kudo2/14kudo2-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/18/opinion/14kudo2/14kudo2-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/18/opinion/14kudo2/14kudo2-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Fought in Afghanistan. I Still Wonder, Was It Worth It?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Was Our Afghan War Worth It?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-14T19:45:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Kudo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kudo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0170fd6-230e-5a54-8dd5-3a7001a915ce', 'word_count': 1644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0170fd6-230e-5a54-8dd5-3a7001a915ce'}, {'abstract': 'Skin care products to try at home for a radiant complexion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/14/style/self-care/glowing-skin-for-your-wedding-day-no-spa-appointment-necessary.html', 'snippet': 'Skin care products to try at home for a radiant complexion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The pandemic might have made it harder to visit a skin-care professional for a facial or other treatments, but you can still achieve that wedding-day glow at home with an assortment of products and even massages that you can do yo