, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Sean (1966- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-15T11:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f0a419d-9023-5943-951d-4f11373ccbae', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f0a419d-9023-5943-951d-4f11373ccbae'}, {'abstract': 'After upending her life, a woman runs away with her longtime crush in this puzzling Japanese drama.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/15/movies/ride-or-die-review.html', 'snippet': 'After upending her life, a woman runs away with her longtime crush in this puzzling Japanese drama.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The long take that opens “Ride or Die” might recall the Steadicam shot in “Goodfellas” were it not for the unsettling mood it evokes. On a clear evening in Tokyo, Rei (Kiko Mizuhara) enters an underground club and buys a stranger a tequila shot. Agitation builds as Rei and the man retire to his condo and start to have sex. Finally, the tension breaks — not in orgasm, but in grisly murder as Rei slits the man’s throat.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/17/arts/ride1/merlin_186182577_0c925c2c-7c9d-421d-a444-2923688f4c7f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/17/arts/ride1/merlin_186182577_0c925c2c-7c9d-421d-a444-2923688f4c7f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/