', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Levenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0091ac4b-9315-5eaa-9044-9c6a37560b64', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0091ac4b-9315-5eaa-9044-9c6a37560b64'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections that appeared in print on Friday, April 16, 2021.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/15/pageoneplus/corrections-april-16-2021.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections that appeared in print on Friday, April 16, 2021.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An article on Thursday about Coinbase’s stock market arrival misspelled the name of a blockchain platform. It is Ethereum, not Ethererum. The article also may have implied incorrectly that Bitcoin is likely to shift to a proof-of-stake model. While some critics say Bitcoin will eventually need to make the switch, there are no plans to do so, and the idea is broadly unpopular within the Bitcoin community.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: April 16, 2021', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-04-16T01:47:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ebb3f41-acf4-5d0a-892c-63b4eae7acf6', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ebb3f41-acf4-5d0a-892c-63b4eae7acf6'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Friday, April 16, 2021.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/15/todayspaper/quotation-of-the-day-feeding-hate-with-video.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Friday, April 16, 2021.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We realized that if we wanted a future on YouTube, it had to be driven by confrontation.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: Feeding Hate With Video', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-04-16T01:48:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/5aa04129-9294-5259-8bf4-91a0db0c87a0', 'word_count': 36, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5aa04129-9294-5259-8bf4-91a0db0c87a0'}, {'abstract': 'Middle and high school students are invited to tell us what they’re reading in The Times and why. The contest begins on June 11.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/15/learning/our-12th-annual-summer-reading-contest.html', 'snippet': 'Middle and high school students are invited to tell us what they’re reading in The Times and why. The contest begins on June 11.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This announcement is available as a one-page PDF to hang on your class bulletin board.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/19/books/review/20Beckerman-LN/20Beckerman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/19/books/review/20Beckerman-LN/20Beckerman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/19/books/review/20Beckerman-LN/20Beckerman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/19/books/review/20Becker