erama Dome (Los Angeles, Calif, Movie Theater)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prince-Bythewood, Gina', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-16T14:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nancy Coleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Coleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b586ee3f-c8bd-5490-aff1-15f899c41755', 'word_count': 893, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b586ee3f-c8bd-5490-aff1-15f899c41755'}, {'abstract': 'The drama dares to show sympathy for an emotionally distant patriarch and his relatively powerless wife — figures familiar to this child of immigrants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/16/movies/minari-korean-americans.html', 'snippet': 'The drama dares to show sympathy for an emotionally distant patriarch and his relatively powerless wife — figures familiar to this child of immigrants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Growing up, I never saw my Korean-American parents touch each other. No hugs or kisses, or even pats on the back. It wasn’t the byproduct of a loveless marriage, just the consequences of a life centered on survival — that endless list of unsexy chores. I’ve lived 30 years without acknowledging such biographical details, accepting that the nuances of my life could never make it into mainstream culture.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/18/arts/18minari-notebook/18minari-notebook-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/18/arts/18minari-noteboo