sh to it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the American Library Association released its list of the 10 most frequently banned or challenged books of 2020, it was no surprise to Angie Thomas that her debut novel, “The Hate U Give,” had made its return to the list for a third appearance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/15/multimedia/15xp-books1/merlin_145436820_7eab613f-5ef9-4c7b-a163-a9a7fb520d92-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/15/multimedia/15xp-books1/merlin_145436820_7eab613f-5ef9-4c7b-a163-a9a7fb520d92-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/15/multimedia/15xp-books1/merlin_145436820_7eab613f-5ef9-4c7b-a163-a9a7fb520d92-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/15/multimedia/15xp-books1/merlin_145436820_7eab613f-5ef9-4c7b-a163-a9a7fb520d92-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1377, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/15/multimedia/15xp-books1/merlin_145436820_7eab613f-5ef9-4c7b-a163-a9a7fb520d92-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/15/multimedia/15xp-books1/merlin_145436820_7eab613f-5ef9-4c7b-a163-a9a7fb520d92-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/15/multimedia/15xp-books1/merlin_145436820_7eab613f-5ef9-4c7b-a163-a9a7fb520d92-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Books About Racism and Police Violence Fill Out List of ‘Most Challenged’ Titles', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN LIBRARY ASSN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kendi, Ibram X', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reynolds, Jason (Author)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Angie (Author)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'All American Boys (Book)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Stamped: Racisim, Antiracism, and You (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Hate U Give (Book)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-16T14:04:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Express', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allyson Waller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allyson', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c5f8a30-9502-5d7a-b150-da12f0783702', 'word_count': 995, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c5f8a30-9502-5d7a-b150-da12f0783702'}, {'abstract': 'The designer Rachel Scott has honed her skills at brands in Milan and New York, but when it came to creating her own label, Diotima, she looked homeward to Jamaica.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/16/t-magazine/diotima-rachel-scott-fashion.html', 'snippet': 'The designer Rachel Scott has honed her skills at brands in Milan and New York, but when it came to creating her own label, Diotima, she looked homeward to Jamaica.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a teen in 1990s Kingston, Jamaica, the fashion designer Rachel Scott was acutely aware of the tension between the decorum dictated by her Jesuit high school, where skirt lengths were checked on a regular basis, and the liberating dancehall scene she was swept up into at night. “There was this idea of being proper and having to present a certain way in the daytime — it was ridiculous,” says Scott, 37, speaking over Zoom from the lush green garden of her family’s house in Kingston, where she is visiting. But the soundtrack of her adolescence — the hip-swaying hits of local artists like Lady Saw, Shabba Ranks and Chaka Demus & Pliers that she heard at parties — left the more lasting impression. “Dancehall will forever be influential to me,” she says of the genre, which has roots in music of the African diaspora. “It’s like this explosion of exuberance.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/15/t-magazine/15tmag-diotima-slide-4513-copy/15tmag-diotima-slide-4513-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/15/t-magazine/15tmag-diotima-slide-4513-copy/15tmag-diotima-slide-4513-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/15/t-magazine/15tmag-diotima-slide-4513-copy/15tmag-diotima-slide-4513-copy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/15/t-magazine/15tmag-diotima-slide-4513-copy/15tmag-diotima-slide-4513-copy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1