 willowy Freya Lyell, who becomes entangled with Byrne Hall and its inhabitants. Freya, bookish and sensible, has always lived in the shadow of her “frightening and beautiful” elder sister, Stella, and never more so since Stella’s body was discovered near the seaside village of Bligh. Five years later Freya, now 23, travels to Bligh from London for a wedding reception at Byrne Hall, only to discover a portrait of Stella hanging on a wall. This portrait, and the artist who painted it — Cory Byrne — launch Freya into the mystery of what really happened to Stella.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/18/books/review/18Horror-Trussoni/18Horror-Trussoni-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/18/books/review/18Horror-Trussoni/18Horror-Trussoni-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/18/books/review/18Horror-Trussoni/18Horror-Trussoni-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/18/books/review/18Horror-Trussoni/18Horror-Trussoni-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1272, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/18/books/review/18Horror-Trussoni/18Horror-Trussoni-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/18/books/review/18Horror-Trussoni/18Horror-Trussoni-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thu