s in 2018. The percentages given referred to homeownership within those communities, not to homeownership in the city over all. That year, 44 percent of Asian households and 43 percent of white households owned their homes, while the same was true for just 27 percent of Black households and 17 percent of Latino households.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: April 17, 2021', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-04-17T01:27:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/55784ea2-8f04-5130-b05e-a81cc288b9da', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55784ea2-8f04-5130-b05e-a81cc288b9da'}, {'abstract': 'President Biden welcomed Prime Minister Yoshihide Suga of Japan to the White House, where they pledged to work together to counter authoritarianism and advance “shared democratic norms.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/100000007715163/biden-japan-prime-minister-suga.html', 'snippet': 'President Biden welcomed Prime Minister Yoshihide Suga of Japan to the White House, where they pledged to work together to counter authoritarianism and advance “shared democratic norms.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Biden welcomed Prime Minister Yoshihide Suga of Japan to the White House, where they pledged to work together to counter authoritarianism and advance “shared democratic norms.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/16/us/politics/16new-washington-briefing-japanese-prim2/merlin_186503382_c070174c-d069-4018-8cab-991e24c9c8d1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 