o approach this. I have offered the widow help with errands when I see her, so she knows we’re here for her, but she declines, and I don’t think that would really help anyway. Any advice on how we can handle this?', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/18/realestate/17Ask--illo/17Ask--illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 118, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/18/realestate/17Ask--illo/17Ask--illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 118}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/18/realestate/17Ask--illo/17Ask--illo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 201, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/18/realestate/17Ask--illo/17Ask--illo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/18/realestate/17Ask--illo/17Ask--illo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/18/realestate/17Ask--illo/17Ask--illo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/18/realestate/17Ask--illo/17Ask--illo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Help a Grieving Neighbor', 'kicker': 'Ask Real Estate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Can I Help a Grieving Neighbor Who Declines Offers of Assistance?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grief (Emotion)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Content Type: Service', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-17T14:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronda Kaysen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaysen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3edc85ed-369d-53ff-bd64-660e6bcd5baf', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3edc85ed-369d-53ff-bd64-660e6bcd5baf'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Times examined survey and vaccine administration data for nearly every U.S. county and found that both willingness to receive a vaccine and actual vaccination rates to date were lower, on average, in counties where a majority of residents voted to re-elect former President Donald J. Trump in 2020.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/17/world/in-counties-that-voted-for-trump-fewer-people-are-getting-vaccinated.html', 'snippet': '', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times examined survey and vaccine administration data for nearly every U.S. county and found that both willingness to receive a vaccine and actual vaccination rates to date were lower, on average, in counties where a majority of residents voted to re-elect former President Donald J. Trump in 2020.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In counties that voted for Trump, fewer people are getting vaccinated.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'internal-essential', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-17T14:17:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Ivory, Lauren Leatherby and Robert Gebeloff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ivory', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leatherby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gebeloff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5445078f-4229-564a-b1d5-2f80ac3b4c63', 'word_count': 51, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5445078f-4229-564a-b1d5-2f80ac3b4c63'}, {'abstract': 'It’s a great time for peas, whether you pair them with pasta or with rice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/17/admin/shine-a-spotlight-on-peas.html', 'snippet': 'It’s a great time for peas, whether you pair them with pasta or with rice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Asparagus and rhubarb steal much of the spotlight this time of year, leaving the modest pea waiting in the wings. Now is its time to shine — in Melissa Clark’s pasta primavera, our most popular recipe of the week, or in this recipe for risi e bisi, the latest from Gabrielle Hamilton. Even its cousin, the sugar snap pea, deserves some time in the sun with Melissa Clark’s spiced salmon with sugar snap peas and red onion (above). You’ll find plenty more dishes packed with spring flavors in our collection of the most popular New York Times Cooking recipes of the week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/09/dining/09appetite