e9'}, {'abstract': 'He wrote prodigiously while teaching, first in Dublin and then in New York, and often clashed with critics he considered too political.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/17/books/denis-donoghue-dead.html', 'snippet': 'He wrote prodigiously while teaching, first in Dublin and then in New York, and often clashed with critics he considered too political.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Denis Donoghue, an Irish academic whose wide-ranging literary tastes, erudite analysis of poets like T.S. Eliot and William Butler Yeats, and fierce aversion to the impositions of postmodern theory earned him a reputation as one of the last great humanist critics, died on April 6 at his home in Durham, N.C. He was 92.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/20/obituaries/17Donoghue/merlin_186483909_88ba04e7-6dff-4fc6-a25f-0484198976f4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/20/obituaries/17Donoghue/merlin_186483909_88ba04e7-6dff-4fc6-a25f-0484198976f4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/20/obituaries/17Donoghue/merlin_186483909_88ba04e7-6dff-4fc6-a25f-0484198976f4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/20/obituaries/17Donoghue/merlin_186483909_88ba04e7-6dff-4fc6-a25f-0484198976f4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1359, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/20/obituaries/17Donoghue/