hed on Saturday and caught fire with neither of the men behind the wheel, the authorities said.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/20/multimedia/18xp-tesla-02/18xp-tesla-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 339, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/20/multimedia/18xp-tesla-02/18xp-tesla-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 339}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/20/multimedia/18xp-tesla-02/18xp-tesla-02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 442, 'width': 783, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/20/multimedia/18xp-tesla-02/18xp-tesla-02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 442, 'width': 783, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/20/multimedia/18xp-tesla-02/18xp-tesla-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/20/multimedia/18xp-tesla-02/18xp-tesla-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/20/multimedia/18xp-tesla-02/18xp-tesla-02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '2 Killed in Driverless Tesla Car Crash, Officials Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Driver in Tesla Crash That Killed 2, Officials Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Driverless and Semiautonomous Vehicles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tesla Motors Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harris County (Tex)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Woodlands, The (Tex)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Musk, Elon', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-18T22:12:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Express', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bryan Pietsch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bryan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pietsch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/225aaef9-aeb9-5565-bbd0-767c5bf5fc52', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/225aaef9-aeb9-5565-bbd0-767c5bf5fc52'}, {'abstract': 'Subscriptions may be the rage, but businesses of all sorts are pouring money into advertising — digital most of all.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/18/business/media/subscriptions-advertising-media.html', 'snippet': 'Subscriptions may be the rage, but businesses of all sorts are pouring money into advertising — digital most of all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you wanted to sound smart at a media business conference or sell your start-up over the last couple of years, you’d talk about the rise of digital subscriptions. Netflix and Spotify led the way in getting consumers to pay every month for their content, and The New York Times, The Washington Post and many others followed. By last week, everyone was hawking media subscriptions, from the owners of the SpongeBob SquarePants TV show ($5.99 a month) to the staid newswire Reuters ($35) to my friend Isaac who wanders aimlessly around New York ($7).', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Roaring Twenties, Ads Make a Comeback', 'kicker': 'the media equation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ads, Once Left for Dead, Make a Comeback in the Roaring Twenties', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Advertising and Marketing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-18T22:55:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ec051ed-2664-5dfa-900a-1c98479cc7dc', 'word_count': 1128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ec051ed-2664-5dfa-900a-1c98479cc7dc'}, {'abstract': 'Jay Bruce, a recent arrival, announced his retirement, and the Yankees fell to 5-10, with problems that seem deeper than their struggles with Tampa Bay.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/18/sports/baseball/yankees-tampa-bay-rays-miserable-start.html', 'snippet': 'Jay Bruce, a recent arrival, announced his retirement, and the Yankees fell to 5-10, with problems that seem deeper than their struggles with Tampa Bay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Yankees lost again on Sunday to Tampa Bay, 4-2, a drearily routine result in an oddly lopsided rivalry. The Rays pulled their usual pitching voodoo, with an opener drafted in the 45th round and a closer with no career saves. The pitcher who worked most of the game has one of the slowest fastballs in the sport.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/18/sports/18kepner-1/merlin_186596085_b2bd549f-5a7d-465f-af8a-e5e2739bbbdf-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/18/sports/18kepner-1/merlin_186596085_b2bd549f-5a7d-465f-af8a-e5e2739bbbdf-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/18/sports/18kepner-1/merlin_186596085_b2bd549f-5a7d-465f-af8a-e5e2739bbbdf-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/18/sports/18kepner-1/merlin_186596085_b2bd549f-5a7d-465f-af8a-e5e2739bbbdf-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1395, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/18/sports/18kepner-1/18kepner-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/18/sports/18kepner-1/18kepner-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credi