d in salsa — these stuffed peppers are worth the effort.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/21/magazine/chiles-rellenos-stuffed-peppers-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'Roasted, filled with queso fresco, fried in an egg batter and simmered in salsa — these stuffed peppers are worth the effort.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andrea Serrato teaches English and math, reads tarot cards and, on Sundays, sells big, fat, absurdly delicious chiles rellenos out of her home in East Los Angeles. The poblano chiles are roasted, filled with queso fresco, fried and then simmered in a spicy, garlicky salsa roja. “Everyone I know has a hustle or two on the side,” she said, “and this is one of mine.” Serrato’s tiny business is called Mamis Xiles, and she takes orders for her homemade chiles rellenos by direct message on Instagram, selling each chile on a bed of rice with corn tortillas for $13. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/25/magazine/25mag-eat/25mag-eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/03/25/magazine/25mag-eat/25mag-eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 451}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/25/magazine/25mag-eat/25mag-eat-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/25/magazine/25mag-eat/25mag-eat-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1541, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/25/magazine/25mag-eat/25mag-eat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/03/25/magazine/25mag-eat/25mag-eat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/03/25/magazine/25mag-eat/25mag-eat-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'These Chiles Rellenos Are Absurdly Delicious', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spicy and Special: These chiles rellenos — roasted, filled with queso fresco, fried in an egg batter and simmered in salsa — are worth the effort. ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chili Peppers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-21T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tejal Rao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tejal', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03e374ef-3a34-5689-8662-b82a0b0c5730', 'word_count': 870, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03e374ef-3a34-5689-8662-b82a0b0c5730'}, {'abstract': 'Langston Hughes, Muriel Rukeyser and Toyo Suyemoto help make sense of challenging times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/21/opinion/national-poetry-month.html', 'snippet': 'Langston Hughes, Muriel Rukeyser and Toyo Suyemoto help make sense of challenging times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I don’t write poetry, and until recently, I didn’t read it. Poetry is too beautiful, and I’m too self-conscious to try to create it. So when I was approached by a foundation to create an animated video series for National Poetry Month, I immediately thought no.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/21/autossell/op-poetry-rukeyser-thumb1/op-poetry-rukeyser-thumb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/21/autossell/op-poetry-rukeyser-thumb1/op-poetry-rukeyser-thumb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/21/autossell/op-poetry-rukeyser-thumb1/op-poetry-rukeyser-thumb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/21/autossell/op-poetry-rukeyser-thumb1/op-poetry-rukeyser-thumb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/21/autossell/op-poetry-rukeyser-thumb1/op-poetry-rukeyser-thumb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/21/autossell/op-poetry-rukeyser-thumb1/op-poetry-rukeyser-thumb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/21/autossell/op-poetry-rukeyser-thumb1/op-poetry-rukeyser-thumb1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Thank Goodness for Poetry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hughes, Langston', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rukeyser, Muriel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suyemoto, Toyo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paredez, Deborah', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matejka, Adrian', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rekdal, Paisley', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-21T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d52b3c27-07a8-5a4d-a94b-b0bef08d2451', 'word_count': 569, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d52b3c27-07a8-5a4d-a94b-b0bef08d2451'}, {'abstract': 'It’s carbon-free, but has a history of disasters. Investing more in nuclear power can help get us to carbon-neutral by 2050. But is it worth it?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/21/opinion/nuclear-power-climate-change.html', 'snippet': 'It’s carbon-free, but has a history of disasters. Investing more in nuclear power can help get us to carbon-neutral by 2050. But is it worth it?', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Biden has set an ambitious goal for the United States to be carbon-neutral by 2050. Achieving it means weaning the country off fossil fuels and using more alternative energy sources like solar and wind. But environmentalists disagree about whether nuclear power should be part of the mix.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/23/opinion/21argument-nuclear-image/21argument-nuclear-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/23/opinion/21argument-nuclear-image/21argument-nuclear-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/23/opinion/21argument-nuclear-image/21argument-nuclear-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/23/opinion/21argument-nuclear-image/21argument-nuclear-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/23/opinion/21argument-nuclear-image/21argument-nuclear-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/23/opinion/21argument-nuclear-image/21argument-nuclear-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/23/opinion/21argument-nuclear-image/21argument-nuclear-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Should America Go Nuclear?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Wastes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nuclear Regulatory Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wind Power', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-21T09:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': "By ‘The Argument'", 'person': [], 'organization': "The Argument'"}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/437fc5b0-4b80-58b2-85cc-919267f3c0bb', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/437fc5b0-4b80-58b2-85cc-919267f3c0bb'}, {'abstract': 'You don’t hear his name as much. But as far as the G.O.P. is concerned, the former president rules.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/21/opinion/trump-republicans.html', 'snippet': 'You don’t hear his name as much. But as far as the G.O.P. is concerned, the former president rules.', 'lead_paragraph': 'His exile in Mar-a-Lago notwithstanding, Donald Trump’s authority over the Republican Party remains vast. You can see it in Republican reluctance to back a bipartisan inquiry into the Jan. 6 Capitol riot, in the widespread denunciation of party members who refused to overturn election results and who voted for Trump’s second impeachment, and in poll data showing continuing repudiation among loyal Republicans of the 2020 election results.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/21/opinion/21edsall-lead/merlin_178004712_f952dacc-447c-45bf-8b7c-55c624a26404-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/21/opinion/21edsall-lead/merlin_178004712_f952dacc-447c