 People', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whites', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Right-Wing Extremism and Alt-Right', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arceneaux, Kevin (Vin)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haley, Nikki R', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-21T09:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas B. Edsall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d563b65e-5fc7-534d-a444-9f3a679688c8', 'word_count': 2753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d563b65e-5fc7-534d-a444-9f3a679688c8'}, {'abstract': 'The past year has changed alcohol use patterns, especially among women. The impacts probably won’t be fully known for years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/21/magazine/covid-drinking-alcohol-health.html', 'snippet': 'The past year has changed alcohol use patterns, especially among women. The impacts probably won’t be fully known for years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even before the pandemic began, some Americans were drinking significantly more alcohol than they had in decades past — with damaging consequences. In 2020, researchers at the National Institute on Alcohol Abuse and Alcoholism (N.I.A.A.A.) found that from 1999 through 2017, per capita consumption increased by 8 percent and the number of alcohol-related deaths doubled, many caused by liver disease. The trends are particularly concerning for women: Whereas the number of men who reported any drinking stayed mostly the same, the proportion of women who did so increased 10 percent, and the number of women who reported binge drinking, or consuming roughly four or more drinks in about two hours, increased by 23 percent. (For men, binge drinking is about five or more drinks in that period.) Current dietary guidelines consider moderate drinking to be at most one drink a day for women and two for men.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/25/magazine/25Mag-StudiesShow-02/25Mag-StudiesShow-02-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/25/magazine/25Mag-StudiesShow-02/25Mag-StudiesShow-02-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/25/magazine/25Mag-StudiesShow-02/25Mag-StudiesShow-02-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/25/magazine/25Mag-StudiesShow-02/25Mag-StudiesShow-02-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/25/magazine/25Mag-StudiesShow-02/25Mag-StudiesShow-02-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/25/magazine/25Mag-StudiesShow-02/25Mag-StudiesShow-02-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/25/magazine/25Mag-StudiesShow-02/25Mag-StudiesShow-02-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Bad Is Our Pandemic Drinking Problem?', 'kicker': 'Studies Show', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The pandemic has changed drinking patterns, especially among women. The impacts probably won’t be fully known for years.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alcohol Abuse', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institute on Alcohol Abuse and Alcoholism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-21T09:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Tingley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tingley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e68fe336-ff9b-5aa4-9065-2e4d07f99ecc', 'word_count': 1334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e68fe336-ff9b-5aa4-9065-2e4d07f99ecc'}, {'abstract': 'The trial of Brendan Hunt, an avid Trump backer and New York City resident, will be one of the justice system’s first attempts to grapple with the events of Jan. 6.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/21/nyregion/brendan-hunt-capitol-riot.html', 'snippet': 'The trial of Brendan Hunt, an avid Trump backer and New York City resident, will be one of the justice system’s first attempts to grapple with the events of Jan. 6.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two days after the attack on the U.S. Capitol, a 37-year-old man living in New York City posted a video online entitled “KILL YOUR SENATORS.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/01/21/nyregion/00threatstrial/00threatstrial-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/01/21/nyregion/00threatstrial/00threatstrial-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/01/21/nyregion/00threatstrial/00threatstrial-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 913, 'width': 685, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/01/21/nyregion/00threatstrial/00threatstrial-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 913, 'width': 685, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/01/21/nyregion/00threatstrial/00threatstrial-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/01/21/nyregion/00threatstrial/00threatstrial-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/01/21/nyregion/00threatstrial/00threatstrial-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'He Said to ‘Kill Your Senators’ in an Online Video. Now He’s on Trial.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Kill Your Senators’ Post Could Put Man in Prison', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Storming of the US Capitol (Jan, 2021)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Right-Wing Extremism and Alt-Right', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hunt, Brendan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-21T09:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Hong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5160a8fc-5999-5cf9-b7ab-251a4ee3cee2', 'word_count': 1256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5160a8fc-5999-5cf9-b7ab-251a4ee3cee2'}, {'abstract': 'Covid fuels the current virus pandemic, but the world is full of flu viruses waiting in the wings. And they keep changing unpredictably.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/21/science/bird-flu-pandemic.html', 'snippet': 'Covid fuels the current virus pandemic, but the world is full of flu viruses waiting in the wings. And they keep changing unpredictably.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a bird flu virus struck a major poultry farm in Russia earlier this year, it was a reminder that the coronavirus causing the pandemic was not the only dangerous virus out there.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/27/science/21SCI-VIRUS-BIRDFLU/21SCI-VIRUS-BIRDFLU-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/27/science/21SCI-VIRUS-BIRDFLU/21SCI-VIRUS-BIRDFLU-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/27/science/21SCI-VIRUS-BIRDFLU/21SCI-VIRUS-BIRDFLU-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/27/science/21SCI-VIRUS-BIRDFLU/21SCI-VIRUS-BIRDFLU-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/27/science/21SCI-VIRUS-BIRDFLU/21SCI-VIRUS-BIRDFLU-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/27/science/21SCI-VIRUS-BIRDFLU/21SCI-VIRUS-BIRDFLU-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/27/science/21SCI-VIRUS-BIRDFLU/21SCI-VIRUS-BIRDFLU-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Bird Flu Jumps to Humans. So Far, It’s Not a Problem.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s Deadly to Birds. It Just Jumped to Humans.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Avian Influenza', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poultry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lucey, Daniel R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Astrakhan (Russia)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-healthcare', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-21T09:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Gorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae76e001-3c94-5dec-842f-decd23060a78', 'word_count': 939, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae76e001-3c94-5dec-842f-decd23060a78'}, {'abstract': 'Designers are finding ways to stay alive after the economic tailspin caused by the pandemic. But optimism and determination have returned.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/21/fashion/weddings/wedding-dress-industry-pandemic.html', 'snippet': 'Designers are finding ways to stay alive after the economic tailspin caused by the pandemic. But optimism and determination have returned.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before Covid hit, Christine Callahan and Samantha Brody, the founders of Ella & Oak, a company that focuses on bridal fashion for plus-size women, opened their first pop-up showroom on West 29th Street in Manhattan. Word of mouth spread quickly. The boutique shop, which showcased designers offering sizes 12-32, was busy. One-on-one hourly appointments were filled weeks in advance. Partnerships with other stores were being offered. Designers started approaching them rather than the other way around. The business had netted more than $20,000 in revenue in their first month.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York