', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus Risks and Safety Concerns', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Content Type: Service', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-22T09:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/9aec86e9-c68d-5a37-9ca5-e9468a5ea014', 'word_count': 1743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9aec86e9-c68d-5a37-9ca5-e9468a5ea014'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists know that the intense stress of grieving can affect the body in various ways, but much remains a mystery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/22/well/what-happens-in-the-body-during-grief.html', 'snippet': 'Scientists know that the intense stress of grieving can affect the body in various ways, but much remains a mystery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1987, when my 18-year-old son was killed in a train accident, a chaplain and two detectives came to my house to notify me. I didn’t cry then, but a wall came down in my mind and I could do nothing except be polite and make the necessary decisions. When friends and relatives showed up, I was still polite, but the wall had now become an infinite darkness and I was obviously in shock, so they took over, helping me to eat and notify people and write death notices.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/20/well/00well-grief-biology-promo/00well-grief-biology-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/20/well/00well-grief-biology-promo/00well-grief-biology-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/20/well/00well-grief-biology-promo/00well-grief-biology-promo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/20/well/00well-grief-biology-promo/00well-grief-biology-promo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/20/well/00well-grief-biology-promo/00well-grief-biology-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/20/well/00well-grief-biology-promo/00well-grief-biology-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/20/well/00well-grief-biology-promo/00well-grief-biology-promo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Biology of Grief', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None