for extra cash that she saves for the two sons waiting for her in Poland. Her stony face never betrays any sign of pleasure, but Josef is clearly satisfied; by the second act, Wanda is pregnant with his child.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/22/crosswords/22WONDERFUL-PIX/merlin_186504114_8e5e0237-2e37-49bf-b3da-10a409e89e3f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/22/crosswords/22WONDERFUL-PIX/merlin_186504114_8e5e0237-2e37-49bf-b3da-10a409e89e3f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/22/crosswords/22WONDERFUL-PIX/merlin_186504114_8e5e0237-2e37-49bf-b3da-10a409e89e3f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/22/crosswords/22WONDERFUL-PIX/merlin_186504114_8e5e0237-2e37-49bf-b3da-10a409e89e3f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/22/crosswords/22WONDERFUL-PIX/22WONDERFUL-PIX-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/22/crosswords/22WONDERFUL-PIX/22WONDERFUL-PIX-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/22/crosswords/22WONDERFUL-PIX/22WONDERFUL-PIX-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘My Wonderful Wanda’ Review: The Secret Life of a Caretaker', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My Wonderful Wanda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keller, Marthe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'My Wonderful Wanda (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oberli, Bettina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-22T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kristen Yoonsoo Kim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kristen', 'middlename': 'Yoonsoo', 'lastname': 'Kim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/afe7f3cb-5c15-59cc-8902-5aade6b27656', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afe7f3cb-5c15-59cc-8902-5aade6b27656'}, {'abstract': 'The German artist and filmmaker Ulrike Ottinger takes us on an unhurried journey through her past.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/22/movies/paris-calligrammes-review.html', 'snippet': 'The German artist and filmmaker Ulrike Ottinger takes us on an unhurried journey through her past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The German artist and filmmaker Ulrike Ottinger, whose work is not nearly as well distributed in the United States as it ought to be, is not generally known for sentimentality. Her long, searching films are elaborately costumed and visionary not-quite allegories of queer radical feminism. Representative titles include “Madame X: An Absolute Ruler” (1982), “The Image of Dorian Gray in the Yellow Press” (1984) and “Joan of Arc of Mongolia” (1992). She can’t be blamed for getting at least a little wistful, though, in her new “Paris Calligrammes,” an autobiographical documentary. It’s about Paris, after all — her Paris, first experienced in the early 1960s.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/22/arts/22paris-calligrammes/merlin_186504258_2e32f39f-7e51-4c3d-aec8-d856d2db4822-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 882, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/22/arts/22paris-calligrammes/merlin_186504258_2e32f39f-7e51-4c3d-aec8-d856d2db4822-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 882}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/22/arts/22paris-calligrammes/merlin_186504258_2e32f39f-7e51-4c3d-aec8-d856d2db4822-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 697, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/22/arts/22paris-calligrammes/merlin_186504258_2e32f39f-7e51-4c3d-aec8-d856d2db4822-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1394, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/22/arts/22paris-calligrammes/22paris-calligrammes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/22/arts/22paris-calligrammes/22paris-calligrammes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/22/arts/22paris-calligrammes/22paris-calligrammes-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Paris Calligrammes’ Review: Recalling the 1960s With Fondness and Passion', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Pick', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Her Paris, Heavy on Characters and Anecdotes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Content Type: Personal Profile', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Paris Calligrammes (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ottinger, Ulrike', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-22T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/96e439b6-cd87-5db0-be33-ec1bf37a8410', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96e439b6-cd87-5db0-be33-ec1bf37a8410'}, {'abstract': 'A conservative father who could not accept his son’s sexuality is led on a contemplative tour of queer life in New York in this Bolivian film.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/22/movies/tu-me-manques-review.html', 'snippet': 'A conservative father who could not accept his son’s sexuality is led on a contemplative tour of queer life in New York in this Bolivian film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Bolivian film “Tu Me Manques” begins with a fight for an absent man’s affection. Jorge (Oscar Martínez) was the father of Gabriel, the former lover of Sebastian (Fernando Barbosa). When a chance phone call makes it possible for Jorge and Sebastian to meet, Sebastian is quick to hurl accusations at Jorge, who wouldn’t accept his son’s sexuality. Jorge has o