g climate change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To kick off Earth Day, the Biden administration hosted an international climate summit to raise awareness of the increasing impacts of global warming. Leaders from all over the globe renewed their dedication to fighting climate change.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/22/us/22new-washington-briefing-climate-roundup/merlin_186753990_b5a13cc0-728f-4fd6-843b-d57016d57748-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/22/us/22new-washington-briefing-climate-roundup/merlin_186753990_b5a13cc0-728f-4fd6-843b-d57016d57748-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/22/us/22new-washington-briefing-climate-roundup/merlin_186753990_b5a13cc0-728f-4fd6-843b-d57016d57748-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/22/us/22new-washington-briefing-climate-roundup/merlin_186753990_b5a13cc0-728f-4fd6-843b-d57016d57748-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/22/us/22new-washington-briefing-climate-roundup/22new-washington-briefing-climate-roundup-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/22/us/22new-washington-briefing-climate-roundup/22new-washington-briefing-climate-roundup-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/22/us/22new-washington-briefing-climate-roundup/22new-washington-briefing-climate-roundup-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Highlights From Day 1 of the International Climate Summit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earth Day', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-22T19:01:34+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maya Blackstone and Taylor Turner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blackstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Taylor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/bc9430b0-01ba-539c-a5d0-0bf634d1a84d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/bc9430b0-01ba-539c-a5d0-0bf634d1a84d'}, {'abstract': 'The musician and memoirist rediscovered this favorite from her childhood while on a recent trip to Seoul.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/22/t-magazine/michelle-zauner-recipe-crying-hmart.html', 'snippet': 'The musician and memoirist rediscovered this favorite from her childhood while on a recent trip to Seoul.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During a three-week visit to Seoul in May 2019, the musician Michelle Zauner saw the city in a nostalgic light. She was staying in an apartment in the Gangnam district to complete the first draft of her memoir, “Crying in H Mart,” following a tour in Asia with her solo indie-pop project, Japanese Breakfast. Though Zauner, 32, grew up in Eugene, Ore., she was born in Seoul, and revisiting the food of her childhood — particularly dotorimuk-muchim, or seasoned acorn jelly, which she ordered often from a noodle restaurant near the apartment — caused new emotions to surface. Traditionally made from foraged acorns that are shelled, dried, ground into a powdery starch, cooked in water and served cold as banchan, or a side dish, its gelatinous texture and earthy flavor triggered a visceral response, first at her fingertips, then on her tongue. “It reminded me of my enduring struggle as a child to keep the slippery bricks between my chopsticks,” Zauner says, adding that the dish is “almost like a Korean aspic, but healthier.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/19/t-magazine/19tmag-zauner/19tmag-zauner-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/19/t-magazine/19tmag-zauner/19tmag-zauner-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/19/t-magazine/19tmag-zauner/19tmag-zauner-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/19/t-magazine/19tmag-zauner/19tmag-zauner-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/19/t-magazine/19tmag-zauner/19tmag-zauner-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subT