 is a stark change in policy at HUD, where then-Secretary Ben Carson once expressed concerns about “big, hairy men” gaining access to women’s shelters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/22/us/transgender-homeless-biden-trump.html', 'snippet': 'The action is a stark change in policy at HUD, where then-Secretary Ben Carson once expressed concerns about “big, hairy men” gaining access to women’s shelters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Biden administration on Thursday withdrew a rule proposed by the Trump administration that would have allowed single-sex homeless shelters to exclude transgender people from facilities that correspond with their gender identity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/22/us/22new-washington-briefing-HUD-transgender/merlin_185190579_07abd803-a7b1-43d9-b3f3-e4f886c1aaeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/22/us/22new-washington-briefing-HUD-transgender/merlin_185190579_07abd803-a7b1-43d9-b3f3-e4f886c1aaeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/22/us/22new-washington-briefing-HUD-transgender/merlin_185190579_07abd803-a7b1-43d9-b3f3-e4f886c1aaeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/22/us/22new-washington-briefing-HUD-transgender/merlin_185190579_07abd803-a7b1-43d9-b3f3-e4f886c1aaeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/22/us/22new-washington-briefing-HUD-transgender/merlin_185190579_07abd803-a7b1-43d9-b3f3-e4f886c1aaeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/22/us/22new-washington-briefing-HUD-transgender/merlin_185190579_07abd803-a7b1-43d9-b3f3-e4f886c1aaeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/22/us/22new-washington-briefing-HUD-transgender/merlin_185190579_07abd803-a7b1-43d9-b3f3-e4f886c1aaeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Biden administration withdraws Trump-era proposal restricting transgender people in homeless shelters.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexuals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Housing and Urban Development Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-22T21:44:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Cameron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cameron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84bd0ff0-fab9-56d7-87ec-64f84c90f8b0', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84bd0ff0-fab9-56d7-87ec-64f84c90f8b0'}, {'abstract': 'Left alone and unconstrained, the British artist has painted throughout the pandemic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/22/t-magazine/rose-wylie-art.html', 'snippet': 'Left alone and unconstrained, the British artist has painted throughout the pandemic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The artist Rose Wylie came of age in austere postwar England, a member of the so-called Silent Generation, but she doesn’t quite fit the mold. While she leads a relatively frugal and hermetic life that exemplifies the resourcefulness her contemporaries are known for, silent she is not. At 86, Wylie paints freewheeling pictures, often with words loosely scrawled across them, that are gloriously big and crude, and full of a certain dry British humor that sends up any whiff of orthodoxy or pretension. Tudor kings and queens cavort cartoonishly across 16-foot-wide, unprimed canvases. Disembodied mouths chomp through exploding cookies. Celebrities, cinematic characters and figures from commercials often appear: stars from Quentin Tarantino films with hulking shoulders and slender legs; Lolita-like blondes in sunglasses; Serena Williams hammering a tennis ball into the air. Nothing is off limits. “I don’t like constraints,” says Wylie. “I’m hugely open to options and possibilities.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/21/t-magazine/art/rose-wylie-slide-7XS2-copy/rose-wylie-slide-7XS2-copy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/21/t-magazine/art/rose-wylie-slide-7XS2-copy/rose-wylie-slide-7XS2-copy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/21/t-magazine/art/rose-wylie-slide-7XS2-copy/rose-wylie-slide-7XS2-copy-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 