gacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/24/opinion/24Dowd1/24Dowd1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/24/opinion/24Dowd1/24Dowd1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/24/opinion/24Dowd1/24Dowd1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/24/opinion/24Dowd1/24Dowd1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Crushed Dream Factory', 'kicker': 'Maureen Dowd', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crushed Dream Factory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-24T15:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maureen Dowd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maureen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dowd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b99e647d-b43f-53d4-a405-5d0511a3736a', 'word_count': 883, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b99e647d-b43f-53d4-a405-5d0511a3736a'}, {'abstract': 'Joan Robinson upended the misogynistic good-old-boys’ network of economists and devised theories around competition and labor vital to the antitrust debates of today.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/24/opinion/joan-robinson-economy-monopoly-labor.html', 'snippet': 'Joan Robinson upended the misogynistic good-old-boys’ network of economists and devised theories around competition and labor vital to the antitrust debates of today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Joan Robinson arrived at Cambridge University in 1929, nobody expected her to become one of the most important economists of the 20th century — let alone the 21st. She had spent the past three of her nearly 26 years in India, where she lived without professional responsibilities while her husband, Austin, an economist six years her senior, tutored a child maharajah. When Austin returned to Britain to join the Cambridge economics faculty, Joan, who had studied the subject as an undergraduate, felt her own ambitions kindled. But she had entered an environment hostile to women.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/26/opinion/26carter-illo/24carter-illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/26/opinion/26carter-illo/24carter-illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/26/opinion/26carter-illo/24carter-illo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/26/opinion/26carter-illo/24carter-illo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/26/opinion/26carter-illo/24carter-illo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/26/opinion/26carter-illo/24carter-illo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/26/opinion/26carter-illo/24carter-illo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Woman Who Shattered the Myth of the Free Market', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robinson, Joan (1903-83)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cambridge University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marshall, Alfred', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keynes, John Maynard', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-24T15:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary D. Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/46a4304d-8b3b-57a4-8384-1a3129a7adba', 'word_count': 1349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46a4304d-8b3b-57a4-8384-1a3129a7adba'}, {'abstract': 'It wouldn’t actually take that much of an investment for Biden to get us headed in the right direction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/24/opinion/climate-change-meatless-meat.html', 'snippet': 'It wouldn’t actually take that much of an investment for Biden to get us headed in the right direction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m a vegan, but I’m also a realist. There’s no chance humanity is going to give up meat, en masse, anytime soon. That said, we can’t just wish away the risks of industrial animal agriculture. If we don’t end this system, soon, terrible things will happen to us and to the planet. Terrible things are already happening.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/25/opinion/25klein-burger/merlin_169265130_e9ce24c7-0f82-46a6-90ac-7fdca689b463-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/25/opinion/25klein-burger/merlin_169265130_e9ce24c7-0f82-46a6-90ac-7fdca689b463-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/25/opinion/25klein-burger/merlin_169265130_e9ce24c7-0f82-46a6-90ac-7fdca689b463-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/25/opinion/25klein-burger/merlin_169265130_e9ce24c7-0f82-46a6-90ac-7fdca689b463-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/25/opinion/25klein-burger/25klein-burger-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/25/opinion/25klein-burger/25klein-burger-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwi