e, the knock is a visceral, even existential, threat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/24/opinion/nomadland-oscars.html', 'snippet': 'For people whose only home is a vehicle, the knock is a visceral, even existential, threat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Spending the first night in my 1995 GMC camper van, I lay awake for hours in my sleeping bag, watching the window shades glow — white, then red, over and over — as cars sped past in the dark. Is that one slowing down? I wondered. Can they see I’m in here? Will they call the cops?', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/26/opinion/26bruder4-inyt/merlin_180423618_4b851c0e-a158-457d-8bc6-2acc6c772a2a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/26/opinion/26bruder4-inyt/merlin_180423618_4b851c0e-a158-457d-8bc6-2acc6c772a2a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/26/opinion/26bruder4-inyt/merlin_180423618_4b851c0e-a158-457d-8bc6-2acc6c772a2a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/26/opinion/26bruder4-inyt/merlin_180423618_4b851c0e-a158-457d-8bc6-2acc6c772a2a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/26/opinion/26bruder4-inyt/25bruder4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/26/opinion/26bruder4-inyt/25bruder4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/26/opinion/26bruder4-inyt/25bruder4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Lived in a Van to Write the Book Behind ‘Nomadland.’ The Fear Is Real.', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Harsh Reality Behind ‘Nomadland’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nomadic People', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recreational Vehicles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Nomadland (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-24T15:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Bruder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a01bd8c-9750-5745-9814-61717de30b24', 'word_count': 997, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a01bd8c-9750-5745-9814-61717de30b24'}, {'abstract': 'What can be done about all of the suffering that remains?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/24/opinion/derek-chauvin-suffering.html', 'snippet': 'What can be done about all of the suffering that remains?', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a wretched and withering year that didn’t so much pass by as scorch through, the guilty verdict in Derek Chauvin’s trial for the murder of George Floyd arrived as a relief. It’s been a long time since it felt as though Americans had the luxury of thinking about the future we want to live in, as opposed to putting out fires in an endless present. In so many respects, we were due for a little hope.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/25/opinion/sunday/24bruenig-lead/merlin_186687522_8ebbc7bf-2202-4c59-90ca-10b80ad33716-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/25/opinion/sunday/24bruenig-lead/merlin_186687522_8ebbc7bf-2202-4c59-90ca-10b80ad33716-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/25/opinion/sunday/24bruenig-lead/merlin_186687522_8ebbc7bf-2202-4c59-90ca-10b80ad33716-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/25/opinion/sunday/24bruenig-lead/merlin_186687522_8ebbc7bf-2202-4c59-90ca-10b80ad33716-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/25/opinion/sunday/24bruenig-lead/24bruenig-lead-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/25/opinion/sunday/24bruenig-lead/24bruenig-lead-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/25/opinion/sunday/24bruenig-lead/24bruenig-lead-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chauvin Was Convicted. Something Is Still Very Wrong.', 'kicker': 'Elizabeth Bruenig', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chauvin Was Convicted, but Suffering Remains', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Criminal Justice', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (Minneapolis, Minn)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chauvin, Derek (1976- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Floyd, George (d 2020)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Lives Matter Movement', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minneapolis (Minn)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-24T15:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Bruenig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruenig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/81826dbe-de58-539e-bca2-9a1fc9b75368', 'word_count': 1182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81826dbe-de58-539e-bca2-9a1fc9b75368'}, {'abstract': 'If the industry won’t change on principle, it can at least change for the money. Reform would enrich people of color, and everyone else.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/24/opinion/hollywood-oscars-racism.html', 'snippet': 'If the industry won’t change on principle, it can at least change for the money. Reform would enrich people of color, and everyone else.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Days after a Minneapolis police officer, Derek Chauvin, suffocated George Floyd and the video went viral, I watched my social media feed fill with blackout tiles and corporate publicity statements. They poured in from every industry, proclaiming solidarity with the Black Lives Matter movement. Hollywood — where I have worked for almost two decades — was no exception.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/25/opinion/sunday/23leonard/23leonard-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/25/opinion/sunday/23leonard/23leonard-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/25/opinion/sunday/23leonard/23leonard-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/25/opinion/sunday/23leonard/23leonard-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/25/opinion/sunday/23leonard/23leonard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/25/opinion/sunday/23leonard/23leonard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/25/opinion/sunday/23leonard/23leonard-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hollywood’s Anti-Black Bias Costs It $10 Billion a Year', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hollywood Bias Comes at a Hefty Price', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-24T15:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Franklin Leonard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Franklin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5717ce14-19c7-502f-b6a2-d1f649d32407', 'word_count': 1411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5717ce14-19c7-502f-b6a2-d1f649d32407'}, {'abstract': 'Emily Cox and Henry Rathvon bring us the forest; can we see the trees?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/24/crosswords/variety-acrostic.html', 'snippet': 'Emily Cox and Henry Rathvon bring us the forest; can we see the trees?', 'lead_paragraph': 'ACROSTIC — Arbor Day is April 30, and I guarantee the timing of this acrostic isn’t coincidental. The passage today is from a really wonderful recent book called “The Overstory,” which won the 2019 Pulitzer Prize in fiction. People who love words and intricate puzzly plots owe it to themselves to try some Richard Powers — I love “The Overstory,” “The Echo Makers” and “The Time of Our Singing,” but you truly can’t go wrong. If you want incredible nature writing with your words and puzzles, start with this book, and read some of it in the shade of a tree for enhancement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Acrostic', 'kicker': 'SUNDAY VARIETY COLUMN', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trees and Shrubs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Powers, Richard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cox, Emily (Crossword Constructor)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rathvon, Henry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-24T16:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caitlin Lovinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caitlin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b51915c-d8f5-5c03-97c7-50d9fb86e674', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b51915c-d8f5-5c03-97c7-50d9fb86e674'}, {'abstract': 'The Turkish government, as well as human rights activists and ethnic Armenians, had a muted response to the news, describing the move as largely symbolic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/24/us/politics/armenia-genocide-joe-biden.html', 'snippet': 'The Turkish government, as well as human rights activists and ethnic Armenians, had a muted response to the news, describing the move as largely symbolic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Biden on Saturday recognized the mass killings of Armenians more than a century ago as genocide, signaling a willingness to test an increasingly frayed relationship with Turkey, long a key regional ally and an important p