ri': 'nyt://article/ac196ab0-29a8-5a64-8929-3a0603ac4804'}, {'abstract': 'The proposed bill, which would prevent intoxication being used as a basis for a plea of insanity, was prompted by a verdict allowing the killer of a Jewish woman to avoid trial.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/26/world/europe/france-anti-semitic-killing-drugs.html', 'snippet': 'The proposed bill, which would prevent intoxication being used as a basis for a plea of insanity, was prompted by a verdict allowing the killer of a Jewish woman to avoid trial.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The French government plans to introduce a bill aimed at closing a legal loophole that allowed the man who killed a Jewish woman in an anti-Semitic frenzy in 2017 to escape trial because a court found that he was in a delirious state brought on by cannabis.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/26/world/26france-jews1/merlin_186885915_9ed1875b-0d25-4eb3-936a-8b3d5d4c5eb4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/26/world/26france-jews1/merlin_186885915_9ed1875b-0d25-4eb3-936a-8b3d5d4c5eb4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/26/world/26france-jews1/merlin_186885915_9ed1875b-0d25-4eb3-936a-8b3d5d4c5eb4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/26/world/26france-jews1/merlin_186885915_9ed1875b-0d25-4eb3-936a-8b3d5d4c5eb4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/26/world/26france-jews1/26france-jews1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/26/world/26france-jews1/26france-jews1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/26/world/26france-jews1/26france-jews1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'France Seeks Change in Law After Outrage Over Verdict in Anti-Semitic Killing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France Seeking to Close Legal Loophole After Protests Over Anti-Semitic Killing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delirium', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Halimi, Sarah (d 2017)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Traore, Kobili', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-26T18:09:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roger Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roger', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d339f75-adb9-58fc-8973-01471f477d24', 'word_count': 644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d339f75-adb9-58fc-8973-01471f477d24'}, {'abstract': 'An exhibition by the painter Elizabeth Downer Riker documents a decade of urban gardening.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/26/dining/elizabeth-downer-riker-urban-farming.html', 'snippet': 'An exhibition by the painter Elizabeth Downer Riker documents a decade of urban gardening.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Re-Enchanting the City,” an exhibition in Chelsea, highlights the visual record of the many vibrant local farms, community gardens and rooftop plantings around the city by the artist Elizabeth Downer Riker. About 10 years ago she started painting rooftop farms in Long Island City, Queens, and parts of Brooklyn, and then took her oils and canvas to other neighborhoods in the city, and even upstate. The exhibition features 20 of her works, and they are for sale, $1,000 to $2,200.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/dining/28BurnerArt/28BurnerArt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/28/dining/28BurnerArt/28BurnerArt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/dining/28BurnerArt/28BurnerArt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/dining/28BurnerArt/28BurnerArt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1351, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/dining/28BurnerArt/28BurnerArt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/28/dining/28BurnerArt/28BurnerArt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/dining/28BurnerArt/28BurnerArt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Urban Farmers Captured on Canvas', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To View: One Painter’s Perspective On Urban Gardening', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-26T18:12:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc95ac45-2cec-5570-9f18-3b67146a5e89', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc95ac45-2cec-5570-9f18-3b67146a5e89'}, {'abstract': 'Pelotón de la Muerte makes three mezcals, and it’s owned in part by the Brooklyn chef Danny Mena.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/26/dining/peloton-de-la-muerte-mezcal.html', 'snippet': 'Pelotón de la Muerte makes three mezcals, and it’s owned in part by the Brooklyn chef Danny Mena.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cinco de Mayo is just around the corner, so you might as well stock up on mezcal like everybody else. (Drizly, an e-commerce liquor retailer, reports that mezcal sales were up 600 percent last year.) Danny Mena, a chef who was notably at Hecho en Dumbo and who is now at La Loncheria in Bushwick, Brooklyn, is also a partner in Pelotón de la Muerte, a mezcal company in Mexico that uses mostly wild magueys (a type of agave) and traditional production methods. The company has three distinctive mezcals made in different regions. Mezcal made from maguey espadín, the most common maguey, has a fruity, pineapple aroma and flavor. The maguey criollo is earthier, smokier and woodsy. And the vegan pechuga mezcal, made from criollo and ancho magueys distilled with citrus, has a burnt orange allure. (Pechuga is usually distilled with chicken breast or other meats but Pelotón de la Muerte uses fruit instead.) This mezcal goes into the cure for savory rustic chorizo-style salami made by New England Charcuterie in Waltham, Mass., and sold at La Loncheria ($9 for 5.5 ounces).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/dining/28BurnerDrink-02/26BurnerDrink-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 474, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/28/dining/28BurnerDrink-02/26BurnerDrink-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 474}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/dining/28BurnerDrink-02/26BurnerDrink-02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 808, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/dining/28BurnerDrink-02/26BurnerDrink-02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1616, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/dining/28BurnerDrink-02/26BurnerDrink-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/28/dining/28BurnerDrink-02/26BurnerDrink-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/dining/28BurnerDrink-02/26BurnerDrink-02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Mezcal With Brooklyn Connections', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Pour: A Mezcal That Has  Brooklyn Connections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alcoholic Beverages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-26T18:16:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f50dd643-22c7-54a1-9f3b-c01608989ae4', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f50dd643-22c7-54a1-9f3b-c01608989ae4'}, {'abstract': 'The writer’s assistant, Laurie Woolever, will discuss their travel book with The New Yorker writer Helen Rosner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/26/dining/anthony-bourdain-book-talk.html', 'snippet': 'The writer’s assistant, Laurie Woolever, will discuss their travel book with The New Yorker writer Helen Rosner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Laurie Woolever, a writer who was the assistant to the peripatetic writer and television personality Anthony Bourdain, has assembled an offbeat yet practical travel guide that the two of them started working on not long before he died in 2018. She soldiered on to assemble the new book, “World Travel: An Irreverent Guide,” based on Mr. Bourdain’s writings and experiences in more than 40 countries. His observations cover the irreverent descriptor with wit to spare, hers touch on practicalities, though you’d never mistake this for Fodor. To better understand it and reminisce about Mr. Bourdain there will be a Zoom discussion of the book with Ms. Woolever and The New Yorker writer Helen Rosner, held by the Museum of Food and Drink.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/dining/28BurnerBook/28BurnerBook-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 740, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/28/dining/28BurnerBook/28BurnerBook-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 740}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/dining/28BurnerBook/28BurnerBook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 830, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/dining/28BurnerBook/28BurnerBook-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1660, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/dining/28BurnerBook/28BurnerBook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/28/dining/28BurnerBook/28BurnerBook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/dining/28BurnerBook/28BurnerBook-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'head