ub_date': '2021-04-27T14:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jolie Ruben, Amanda Webster and Raillan Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jolie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruben', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Raillan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8569b522-c8b4-573f-a320-9566ac107ff7', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8569b522-c8b4-573f-a320-9566ac107ff7'}, {'abstract': 'It feels very American to turn the vaccine rollout into a branding spectacle rooted in the worship of pharmaceutical companies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/27/arts/covid-vaccine-tiktok-content.html', 'snippet': 'It feels very American to turn the vaccine rollout into a branding spectacle rooted in the worship of pharmaceutical companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What is your favorite piece of vaccine-related content? Mine is a TikTok that goes like this: An adult man smiles assuredly at an imaginary group positioned outside the frame. “OK, I’ll see you tomorrow,” he tells them, then swivels to whisper urgently into a phone pressed to his ear. Suddenly his eyeballs are glazed with tears. “Mom, can you come get me,” he pleads. “Yeah, ’cause I freaking hate it here. I’ve been working so hard and I make one mistake and now everyone is like, trying to cancel me. Yeah, and Moderna and Pfizer,” he continues, are the meanest people “I’ve ever met.” A text box tacked to the screen identifies the man as “Johnson & Johnson.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/arts/27VACCINE-CONTENT/27VACCINE-CONTENT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/28/arts/27VACCINE-CONTENT/27VACCINE-CONTENT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/arts/27VACCINE-CONTENT/27VACCINE-CONTENT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/arts/27VACCINE-CONTENT/27VACCINE-CONTENT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/arts/27VACCINE-CONTENT/27VACCINE-CONTENT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/28/arts/27VACCINE-CONTENT/27VACCINE-CONTENT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/arts/27VACCINE-CONTENT/27VACCINE-CONTENT-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Vaccines Become an Internet Personality Test', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Coming Soon: ‘All My Vaccines’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'ra