, 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b64b209d-b13c-5fdb-98b3-7fb5f03789ff', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b64b209d-b13c-5fdb-98b3-7fb5f03789ff'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Secret to Superhuman Strength,” Bechdel chronicles her susceptibility to exercise fads, including karate, yoga, skiing, biking, running, hiking and mountain climbing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/27/books/review-secret-to-superhuman-strength-alison-bechdel.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Secret to Superhuman Strength,” Bechdel chronicles her susceptibility to exercise fads, including karate, yoga, skiing, biking, running, hiking and mountain climbing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early in her career, Alison Bechdel, then a cult cartoonist — “at the pinnacle of my bitterness,” she would later say — was invited to contribute to a special gay pride issue of Seattle’s alternative newspaper The Stranger. She fired off a comic strip titled “Oppressed Minority Cartoonist.” She drew herself at her desk, flanked by a bottle of Scotch, mid-tirade. Why had her work been pigeonholed? And why had she complied so willingly, chronicling only lesbians, her “oppressed minority group”? In the last panel, her rant is interrupted by a phone call inviting her to contribute to that very gay pride issue. “I’d be honored,” she capitulates.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/books/review/27bookbechdel1/27bookbechdel1-articleLarge.png', 'height': 830, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/28/books/review/27bookbechdel1/27bookbechdel1-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 830}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/books/review/27bookbechdel1/27bookbechdel1-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 741, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/books/review/27bookbechdel1/27bookbechdel1-superJumbo.png', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1481, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/books/review/27bookbechdel1/27bookbechdel1-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/04/28/books/review/27bookbechdel1/27bookbechdel1-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/books/review/27bookbechdel1/27bookbechdel1-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alison Bechdel’s Latest Offers Familiar Pleasures in Brighter Colors', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Exploring the Importance  Of Learning How to Fall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Secret to Superhuman Strength (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bechdel, Alison', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-27T19:52:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'origin