m/2021/04/28/us/politics/biden-address-congress-spending.html', 'snippet': 'The president urged lawmakers from both parties to embrace a sweeping new vision for public benefits, financed by higher taxes on the wealthiest Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Biden called for a broad reshaping of American society Wednesday night, using his first formal address to Congress to urge a vast expansion of safety net and educational programs while promising to harness the government to create jobs and opportunity for those often left behind.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Biden calls for a new era of government spending, saying, ‘We can’t stop now.’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'American Rescue Plan (2021)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stimulus (Economic)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-28T21:18:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55f48949-2bc4-59ca-b877-8abbcd91a9cd', 'word_count': 822, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55f48949-2bc4-59ca-b877-8abbcd91a9cd'}, {'abstract': 'The legislation, which now heads back to the State Senate for a vote, would add strict new rules for drop boxes and new identification requirements for absentee ballots, among other measures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/28/us/politics/florida-voting.html', 'snippet': 'The legislation, which now heads back to the State Senate for a vote, would add strict new rules for drop boxes and new identification requirements for absentee ballots, among other measures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A bill that would impose a raft of new restrictions on voting in Florida cleared the State House of Representatives on Wednesday after hours of contentious debate. Democrats denounced the legislation as overly stringent and unnecessary, and Republicans argued that it would install necessary “guardrails” for securing elections, despite their acknowledgment that the state’s election last year had been a “gold standard” without fraud.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/us/politics/28new-washington-briefing-florida-voting-bill/merlin_179414091_6fcdae32-6bef-4a8c-a448-dd4640fc6445-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/04/28/us/politics/28new-washington-briefing-florida-voting-bill/merlin_179414091_6fcdae32-6bef-4a8c-a448-dd4640fc6445-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/us/politics/28new-washington-briefing-florida-voting-bill/merlin_179414091_6fcdae32-6bef-4a8c-a448-dd4640fc6445-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 637, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/04/28/us/politics/28new-washington-briefing-florida-voting-bill/merlin_179414091_6fcdae32-6bef-4a8c-a448-dd4640fc6445-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1274, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo',