: The Story of an Unexpected Friendship and a Beloved Restaurant (Book)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-04-30T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Reese', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reese', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4dec29d-4b20-59df-8232-5adcf9890b49', 'word_count': 897, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4dec29d-4b20-59df-8232-5adcf9890b49'}, {'abstract': 'Six new paperbacks to check out this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/30/books/review/new-paperbacks.html', 'snippet': 'Six new paperbacks to check out this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DOWN THE HIGHWAY: The Life of Bob Dylan, by Howard Sounes. (Grove, 608 pp., $22.) This 20th-anniversary edition celebrating Dylan’s upcoming 80th birthday includes a new chapter by the author on the past 10 years of Dylan’s life. “No matter the time or place,” Perry Meisel wrote in his 2001 review of the book in these pages, “Dylan comes alive, strumming his guitar in a studio in Nashville or hurrying down Macdougal Street with the collar of his leather jacket turned up against the wind.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/02/books/02PAPERROW-COMBO/02PAPERROW-GRID-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 299, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/05/02/books/02PAPERROW-COMBO/02PAPERROW-GRID-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 299}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/05/02/books/02PAPERROW-COMBO/02PAPERROW-GRID-jumbo.